var e={id:`italy`,name:`Italy`,localName:`Italia`,flag:`🇮🇹`,currency:`EUR`,language:`Italian`,greeting:{text:`Ciao!`,meaning:`Hi! / Bye! (informal; use "Buongiorno" in shops and hotels)`},bestMonths:[4,5,6,9,10],tips:[`Many state museums close on Mondays — check opening days before you build an itinerary around one.`,`Book big-name sights (Vatican Museums, Uffizi, Accademia, Borghese, Last Supper) online in advance; walk-up queues can take hours or tickets sell out.`,`Churches enforce a dress code: shoulders and knees covered. A light scarf in your bag solves it.`,`A 'coperto' (cover charge, €1–3) on restaurant bills is normal; tipping beyond rounding up is optional.`,`Regional train tickets bought on paper must be validated in the machines before boarding; e-tickets don't. Coffee standing at the bar is cheaper than sitting at a table.`,`Hotels charge a nightly city tax in cash or card on arrival, and Venice charges day-trippers an access fee on peak dates (overnight guests are exempt but must register).`],cities:[{id:`rome`,name:`Rome`,localName:`Roma`,lat:41.9028,lng:12.4964,timezone:`Europe/Rome`,tagline:`Three thousand years of history, served with cacio e pepe`,description:`The Eternal City layers ancient ruins, Baroque piazzas and Renaissance masterpieces into one walkable, chaotic, delicious whole. Every street corner seems to hide a fountain, a church or a perfect trattoria.`,idealDays:[3,5],places:[{id:`colosseum`,name:`Colosseum`,localName:`Colosseo`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`ancient-rome`,`history`,`unesco`],area:`Colosseo`,lat:41.8902,lng:12.4922,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:5,description:`The 50,000-seat amphitheatre of ancient Rome is still breathtaking in scale. Walk the arena-level galleries and imagine the roar of gladiatorial games.`,tip:`Tickets are timed and nominative — book on the official site weeks ahead; the same ticket covers the Roman Forum and Palatine Hill.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Colosseum`},{id:`roman-forum-palatine`,name:`Roman Forum & Palatine Hill`,localName:`Foro Romano e Palatino`,category:`culture`,tags:[`iconic`,`ancient-rome`,`ruins`,`history`],area:`Colosseo`,lat:41.8925,lng:12.4853,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:5,description:`The political heart of the Roman Empire: temples, triumphal arches and the Senate house, overlooked by the emperors' palaces on the Palatine.`,tip:`Included in the Colosseum combo ticket (valid 24 hours). There's very little shade, so bring water and a hat in summer.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Roman Forum`},{id:`pantheon`,name:`Pantheon`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`ancient-rome`,`architecture`,`rainy-day`],area:`Centro Storico`,lat:41.8986,lng:12.4769,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:6,rating:5,description:`A nearly 1,900-year-old temple whose unreinforced concrete dome and open oculus still astonish engineers. Raphael is buried inside.`,tip:`Entry is about €5; buy online to skip the line. When it rains, watch the water fall through the oculus and drain through the floor.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Pantheon, Rome`},{id:`trevi-fountain`,name:`Trevi Fountain`,localName:`Fontana di Trevi`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`baroque`,`fountain`,`night-view`],area:`Trevi`,lat:41.9009,lng:12.4833,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:2,rating:4,description:`Rome's most theatrical Baroque fountain, where Neptune bursts from a palace façade. Toss a coin over your shoulder to guarantee a return.`,tip:`A small ticket is now charged to reach the basin-side area; come early morning or late evening to avoid the shoulder-to-shoulder crowds.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Trevi Fountain`},{id:`vatican-museums`,name:`Vatican Museums & Sistine Chapel`,localName:`Musei Vaticani e Cappella Sistina`,category:`museum`,tags:[`iconic`,`art`,`michelangelo`,`rainy-day`],area:`Vatican`,lat:41.9065,lng:12.4536,durationHours:3.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:5,description:`Miles of papal collections — the Raphael Rooms, the Gallery of Maps, classical sculpture — culminating in Michelangelo's Sistine Chapel ceiling.`,tip:`Closed Sundays except the last Sunday of the month (free, very crowded). Book the earliest slot online; photos are not allowed in the Sistine Chapel.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Vatican Museums`},{id:`st-peters-basilica`,name:`St. Peter's Basilica`,localName:`Basilica di San Pietro`,category:`culture`,tags:[`iconic`,`church`,`michelangelo`,`free`,`rainy-day`,`viewpoint`],area:`Vatican`,lat:41.9022,lng:12.4539,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`The largest church in Christendom, home to Michelangelo's Pietà and Bernini's bronze baldachin. Climb the dome for a sweeping view over St. Peter's Square.`,tip:`Entry is free but security lines grow fast after 9am. The dome climb (551 steps, or an elevator partway) costs extra.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`St. Peter's Basilica`},{id:`piazza-navona`,name:`Piazza Navona`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`baroque`,`piazza`,`free`,`people-watching`,`night-view`],area:`Centro Storico`,lat:41.8992,lng:12.4731,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`An oval Baroque piazza built on a Roman stadium, anchored by Bernini's Fountain of the Four Rivers. Street artists and musicians bring it alive after dark.`,tip:`The cafés on the square are pricey — grab a drink on a side street like Via del Governo Vecchio instead.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Piazza Navona`},{id:`borghese-gallery`,name:`Borghese Gallery`,localName:`Galleria Borghese`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`bernini`,`caravaggio`,`rainy-day`],area:`Villa Borghese`,lat:41.9142,lng:12.4921,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:5,description:`A jewel-box villa holding Bernini's most dazzling sculptures — Apollo and Daphne, the Rape of Proserpina — plus a room full of Caravaggios.`,tip:`Reservations are mandatory for 2-hour timed slots and sell out days ahead. Closed Mondays.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Galleria Borghese`},{id:`pincio-terrace`,name:`Villa Borghese Gardens & Pincio Terrace`,localName:`Terrazza del Pincio`,category:`nature`,tags:[`park`,`sunset`,`viewpoint`,`free`,`kids`],area:`Villa Borghese`,lat:41.9113,lng:12.4797,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Rome's green lung, with shady avenues, a boating lake and the Pincio balcony overlooking Piazza del Popolo and the domes beyond.`,tip:`Rent a bike or a four-person surrey to cover the park, then time your arrival at the Pincio for sunset.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Villa Borghese gardens`},{id:`trastevere`,name:`Trastevere Evening Stroll`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`neighbourhood`,`dinner`,`bars`,`free`,`night-view`],area:`Trastevere`,lat:41.8894,lng:12.4703,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Ivy-draped lanes, golden-lit piazzas and packed trattorias make Trastevere Rome's favourite place to eat and drink. Start at the glittering mosaics of Santa Maria in Trastevere.`,tip:`Book dinner on weekends; the best trattorias fill by 8:30pm.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Trastevere`},{id:`gianicolo-terrace`,name:`Janiculum Hill Terrace`,localName:`Terrazza del Gianicolo`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`viewpoint`,`sunset`,`free`,`panorama`],area:`Trastevere`,lat:41.892,lng:12.4614,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The finest free panorama of Rome's rooftops and domes, a short uphill walk from Trastevere.`,tip:`A cannon is fired here every day at noon. Walk up via the Acqua Paola fountain.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Janiculum`},{id:`campo-de-fiori`,name:`Campo de' Fiori Market`,category:`food`,tags:[`market`,`produce`,`free`,`piazza`],area:`Centro Storico`,lat:41.8957,lng:12.4722,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A lively open-air market by day and a buzzing bar square by night, watched over by the brooding statue of Giordano Bruno.`,tip:`Market runs Monday–Saturday mornings. Forno Campo de' Fiori on the corner does excellent pizza bianca.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Campo de' Fiori`},{id:`testaccio-market`,name:`Testaccio Market`,localName:`Mercato di Testaccio`,category:`food`,tags:[`market`,`street-food`,`local`,`rainy-day`],area:`Testaccio`,lat:41.8768,lng:12.4752,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:4,description:`A covered neighbourhood market where locals shop and food lovers graze on trapizzini, supplì and fresh pasta in Rome's most authentic food district.`,tip:`Closed Sundays. Stalls start closing around 3pm.`,indoor:!0},{id:`spanish-steps`,name:`Spanish Steps`,localName:`Scalinata di Trinità dei Monti`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`free`,`piazza`,`photo-spot`],area:`Tridente`,lat:41.906,lng:12.4828,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The elegant 135-step staircase rising from Piazza di Spagna to the Trinità dei Monti church, a classic Roman meeting point.`,tip:`Sitting on the steps is banned and fined — enjoy them on your feet.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Spanish Steps`},{id:`via-condotti`,name:`Via dei Condotti & Via del Corso Shopping`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`fashion`,`luxury`,`boutiques`],area:`Tridente`,lat:41.9052,lng:12.48,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Italy's big fashion houses line Via dei Condotti, while parallel Via del Corso offers high-street brands at saner prices.`,tip:`Stop at Antico Caffè Greco (since 1760) on Via dei Condotti for a coffee at the bar.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Via dei Condotti`},{id:`capitoline-museums`,name:`Capitoline Museums`,localName:`Musei Capitolini`,category:`museum`,tags:[`ancient-rome`,`sculpture`,`viewpoint`,`rainy-day`],area:`Campidoglio`,lat:41.893,lng:12.4826,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:18,rating:4,description:`The world's oldest public museum, on Michelangelo's Piazza del Campidoglio, holds the bronze She-Wolf and Marcus Aurelius statue.`,tip:`The Tabularium gallery inside has one of the best views over the Roman Forum.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Capitoline Museums`},{id:`castel-sant-angelo`,name:`Castel Sant'Angelo`,category:`museum`,tags:[`castle`,`viewpoint`,`history`,`kids`],area:`Vatican`,lat:41.9031,lng:12.4663,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:18,rating:4,description:`Hadrian's mausoleum turned papal fortress, with a rooftop terrace overlooking the Tiber and St. Peter's dome.`,tip:`Cross the angel-lined Ponte Sant'Angelo on foot for the classic approach.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Castel Sant'Angelo`},{id:`appian-way-bike`,name:`Appian Way by Bike`,localName:`Via Appia Antica`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`cycling`,`ancient-rome`,`countryside`,`catacombs`],area:`Appia Antica`,lat:41.858,lng:12.516,durationHours:3.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:4,description:`Cycle the 2,300-year-old basalt road past tombs, pines and aqueduct ruins, stopping at the underground Catacombs of San Callisto.`,tip:`Sundays the road is largely closed to cars. Rent bikes (e-bikes help) at the Appia Antica park info point.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Appian Way`},{id:`bioparco`,name:`Bioparco di Roma`,category:`family`,tags:[`zoo`,`kids`,`animals`],area:`Villa Borghese`,lat:41.917,lng:12.4847,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:22,rating:3,description:`Rome's century-old zoo inside Villa Borghese, now focused on conservation, makes an easy break for kids tired of ruins.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Bioparco di Roma`},{id:`ostia-antica`,name:`Ostia Antica Day Trip`,category:`culture`,tags:[`day-trip`,`ancient-rome`,`ruins`,`uncrowded`],area:`Ostia Antica`,lat:41.7557,lng:12.2913,durationHours:4.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:22,rating:4,description:`Rome's ancient seaport is a sprawling, remarkably preserved city of mosaics, taverns, bathhouses and a theatre — often far quieter than the Forum.`,tip:`Reach it in about 40 minutes on the Roma–Lido train from Piramide using a regular metro ticket. Closed Mondays.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Ostia Antica`},{id:`jewish-ghetto`,name:`Jewish Ghetto & Portico d'Ottavia`,localName:`Ghetto Ebraico`,category:`culture`,tags:[`neighbourhood`,`history`,`food`,`free`],area:`Ghetto`,lat:41.8925,lng:12.4776,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Rome's old Jewish quarter wraps around the ruined Portico of Octavia, with kosher bakeries and trattorias famed for crisp deep-fried carciofi alla giudia.`,tip:`Pasticceria Boccione's burnt-edged ricotta and sour-cherry tart is legendary; it's closed on Saturdays for Shabbat.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Roman Ghetto`},{id:`santa-maria-maggiore`,name:`Basilica of Santa Maria Maggiore`,localName:`Basilica di Santa Maria Maggiore`,category:`culture`,tags:[`church`,`mosaics`,`free`,`rainy-day`],area:`Esquilino`,lat:41.8976,lng:12.4984,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`One of Rome's four papal basilicas, glowing with 5th-century mosaics beneath a coffered ceiling said to be gilded with the first gold brought from the Americas.`,tip:`Pope Francis was buried here in 2025, so expect a queue at his tomb; shoulders and knees must be covered.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Santa Maria Maggiore`},{id:`san-clemente`,name:`Basilica of San Clemente`,localName:`Basilica di San Clemente`,category:`culture`,tags:[`church`,`underground`,`hidden-gem`,`rainy-day`],area:`Colosseo`,lat:41.8893,lng:12.4976,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:4,description:`Three layers of history stacked on top of each other: a 12th-century basilica above a 4th-century church above a Roman house and a temple of Mithras.`,tip:`The upper church is free; the paid excavations are the highlight — listen for the underground stream still rushing beneath the lowest level.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Basilica of San Clemente`},{id:`monti`,name:`Monti Neighbourhood`,localName:`Rione Monti`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`neighbourhood`,`aperitivo`,`vintage`,`bars`,`local`],area:`Monti`,lat:41.8955,lng:12.4922,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Rome's oldest district is now its most bohemian: ivy-draped lanes of vintage shops and wine bars around a fountain piazza where locals gather with a drink at dusk.`,tip:`Piazza della Madonna dei Monti is the evening meeting point; Via del Boschetto and Via Urbana have the best independent shops.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Monti (rione of Rome)`},{id:`doria-pamphilj`,name:`Doria Pamphilj Gallery`,localName:`Galleria Doria Pamphilj`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`palace`,`caravaggio`,`rainy-day`,`uncrowded`],area:`Centro Storico`,lat:41.8979,lng:12.4814,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:19,rating:4,description:`A princely family still owns this palace off Via del Corso, whose mirrored galleries hold Velázquez's piercing portrait of Pope Innocent X and early Caravaggios.`,tip:`The audio guide is narrated by a member of the Doria Pamphilj family — witty and personal.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Galleria Doria Pamphilj`},{id:`baths-of-caracalla`,name:`Baths of Caracalla`,localName:`Terme di Caracalla`,category:`culture`,tags:[`ancient-rome`,`ruins`,`uncrowded`,`opera`],area:`Aventino`,lat:41.879,lng:12.4924,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:13,rating:4,description:`The colossal brick shell of a 3rd-century bath complex that served some 1,600 bathers at a time, with surviving mosaic floors underfoot.`,tip:`In summer the ruins host open-air opera and ballet by the Teatro dell'Opera di Roma — a spectacular night out.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Baths of Caracalla`},{id:`aventine-orange-garden`,name:`Aventine Hill & Orange Garden`,localName:`Giardino degli Aranci`,category:`nature`,tags:[`viewpoint`,`sunset`,`free`,`hidden-gem`,`garden`],area:`Aventino`,lat:41.884,lng:12.4794,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A peaceful hilltop garden of bitter-orange trees with a sweeping view to St. Peter's, steps from the Knights of Malta keyhole that frames the dome perfectly.`,tip:`Expect a short queue at the keyhole on Piazza dei Cavalieri di Malta; it moves quickly.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Aventine Hill`},{id:`palazzo-massimo`,name:`Palazzo Massimo alle Terme`,category:`museum`,tags:[`ancient-rome`,`frescoes`,`sculpture`,`rainy-day`,`uncrowded`],area:`Termini`,lat:41.9014,lng:12.4981,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:14,rating:4,description:`The National Roman Museum's finest branch, home to the bronze Boxer at Rest and the dreamlike painted garden from the Empress Livia's villa.`,tip:`The ticket also covers the other National Roman Museum sites, including the Baths of Diocletian nearby.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Palazzo Massimo alle Terme`},{id:`ara-pacis`,name:`Ara Pacis Museum`,localName:`Museo dell'Ara Pacis`,category:`museum`,tags:[`ancient-rome`,`augustus`,`architecture`,`rainy-day`],area:`Tridente`,lat:41.9063,lng:12.4754,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:17,rating:3,description:`Augustus's exquisitely carved Altar of Peace (9 BC), displayed in Richard Meier's glass-and-travertine pavilion beside the emperor's mausoleum.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Ara Pacis`},{id:`mercato-centrale-roma`,name:`Mercato Centrale Roma`,category:`food`,tags:[`food-hall`,`rainy-day`,`late-opening`,`dinner`],area:`Termini`,lat:41.8996,lng:12.501,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:14,rating:3,description:`A vaulted 1930s hall inside Termini station turned into a food court, with counters for trapizzini, Roman pizza, fresh pasta and craft beer.`,tip:`Handy for a late dinner or a meal before an early train — it stays open until around midnight.`,indoor:!0},{id:`villa-deste-tivoli`,name:`Villa d'Este, Tivoli`,category:`nature`,tags:[`day-trip`,`gardens`,`fountains`,`unesco`,`renaissance`],area:`Tivoli`,lat:41.9628,lng:12.796,durationHours:6,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:4,description:`A Renaissance cardinal's terraced garden of hundreds of fountains, cascades and a musical water organ, in the hills east of Rome.`,tip:`Pair it with Hadrian's Villa at the foot of the hill; regional trains and Cotral buses reach Tivoli in about an hour.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Villa d'Este`},{id:`orvieto`,name:`Orvieto Day Trip`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`day-trip`,`hill-town`,`cathedral`,`wine`],area:`Orvieto`,lat:42.7174,lng:12.1131,durationHours:7,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:45,rating:4,description:`An Umbrian hill town perched on a sheer volcanic cliff, crowned by a dazzling striped cathedral and riddled with Etruscan caves below.`,tip:`Trains from Roma Termini take 75–90 minutes; a funicular lifts you from the station up to the old town.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Orvieto`},{id:`explora`,name:`Explora Children's Museum`,localName:`Explora – Il Museo dei Bambini di Roma`,category:`family`,tags:[`kids`,`hands-on`,`rainy-day`],area:`Flaminio`,lat:41.9137,lng:12.4741,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:3,description:`A hands-on play museum near Piazza del Popolo where under-12s run their own mini city, complete with supermarket, post office and fire station.`,tip:`Visits run in timed sessions; book ahead at weekends and in school holidays.`,indoor:!0},{id:`villa-doria-pamphili`,name:`Villa Doria Pamphili Park`,localName:`Villa Doria Pamphili`,category:`nature`,tags:[`park`,`free`,`running`,`picnic`,`kids`],area:`Monteverde`,lat:41.886,lng:12.453,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Rome's largest landscaped park, a 180-hectare sweep of umbrella pines, lawns and fountains where Romans jog, picnic and walk their dogs.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Villa Doria Pamphili`},{id:`vittoriano`,name:`Altar of the Fatherland (Vittoriano)`,localName:`Altare della Patria`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`monument`,`viewpoint`,`free`,`architecture`],area:`Campidoglio`,lat:41.8946,lng:12.4831,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The gleaming white 'wedding cake' monument to Italy's first king towers over Piazza Venezia; its terraces give free views down the Via dei Fori Imperiali.`,tip:`A paid glass lift at the back (Roma dal Cielo) rises to the rooftop for one of the best 360° panoramas in the city.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Victor Emmanuel II Monument`},{id:`porta-portese-market`,name:`Porta Portese Flea Market`,localName:`Mercato di Porta Portese`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`market`,`flea-market`,`vintage`,`sunday`,`free`],area:`Trastevere`,lat:41.8814,lng:12.4728,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Rome's sprawling Sunday flea market stretches for blocks south of Trastevere, a chaos of vintage clothes, antiques, records and bric-a-brac.`,tip:`Sundays only, roughly 7am–2pm; come early for the best finds and keep an eye on your pockets.`,indoor:!1},{id:`st-john-lateran`,name:`Archbasilica of St. John Lateran`,localName:`Basilica di San Giovanni in Laterano`,category:`culture`,tags:[`church`,`free`,`rainy-day`,`history`],area:`San Giovanni`,lat:41.8859,lng:12.5056,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The Pope's own cathedral and the mother church of Catholicism, with Borromini's vast white nave lined by giant marble apostles.`,tip:`Across the square, pilgrims climb the Scala Santa on their knees; a side staircase lets you walk up to the chapel.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Archbasilica of Saint John Lateran`},{id:`capuchin-crypt`,name:`Capuchin Crypt`,localName:`Cripta dei Cappuccini`,category:`culture`,tags:[`macabre`,`hidden-gem`,`rainy-day`],area:`Barberini`,lat:41.9046,lng:12.4888,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:11,rating:3,description:`Six small chapels beneath a Via Veneto church decorated with the bones of some 3,700 friars arranged into chandeliers and arches — eerie and strangely beautiful.`,tip:`Photography isn't allowed in the crypt; the ticket includes a small museum of Capuchin history.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Capuchin Crypt`}],foods:[{name:`Cacio e Pepe`,description:`Tonnarelli tossed with Pecorino Romano and black pepper into a glossy, deceptively simple sauce.`},{name:`Spaghetti alla Carbonara`,localName:`Carbonara`,description:`Egg yolk, guanciale, Pecorino and pepper — never cream in Rome.`},{name:`Supplì`,description:`Fried rice croquettes with a molten mozzarella core, Rome's favourite street snack.`},{name:`Roman-Style Artichokes`,localName:`Carciofi alla Romana / alla Giudia`,description:`Braised with mint and garlic, or deep-fried whole in the Jewish Ghetto style; best in spring.`},{name:`Saltimbocca`,localName:`Saltimbocca alla Romana`,description:`Veal escalopes topped with prosciutto and sage, pan-fried in butter and white wine.`},{name:`Maritozzo`,description:`A soft sweet bun split and stuffed with a cloud of whipped cream, eaten for breakfast.`}]},{id:`florence`,name:`Florence`,localName:`Firenze`,lat:43.7696,lng:11.2558,timezone:`Europe/Rome`,tagline:`The Renaissance, packed into one walkable city`,description:`Cradle of the Renaissance, Florence crams Brunelleschi's dome, Michelangelo's David and Botticelli's Venus into a compact centre on the Arno. Beyond the art, it's a city of leather workshops, wine bars and hearty Tuscan cooking.`,idealDays:[2,4],places:[{id:`duomo`,name:`Florence Cathedral & Brunelleschi's Dome`,localName:`Duomo di Firenze (Santa Maria del Fiore)`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`architecture`,`viewpoint`,`unesco`],area:`Duomo`,lat:43.7731,lng:11.256,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:33,rating:5,description:`The marble-striped cathedral and its colossal brick dome define Florence's skyline. Climb 463 steps past the Last Judgment frescoes to the lantern.`,tip:`The cathedral itself is free, but the dome climb requires the Brunelleschi Pass with a timed slot — book days ahead. The pass also covers the Baptistery, bell tower and museum.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Florence Cathedral`},{id:`uffizi`,name:`Uffizi Gallery`,localName:`Galleria degli Uffizi`,category:`museum`,tags:[`iconic`,`art`,`botticelli`,`rainy-day`],area:`Signoria`,lat:43.7678,lng:11.2553,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:28,rating:5,description:`The world's greatest collection of Renaissance painting: Botticelli's Birth of Venus, Leonardo's Annunciation, Caravaggio and Titian.`,tip:`Closed Mondays. Book a timed entry; early-morning or late-afternoon slots (and cheaper Nov–Feb prices) are calmest.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Uffizi`},{id:`accademia`,name:`Galleria dell'Accademia (Michelangelo's David)`,localName:`Galleria dell'Accademia`,category:`museum`,tags:[`iconic`,`michelangelo`,`sculpture`,`rainy-day`],area:`San Marco`,lat:43.7768,lng:11.2588,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:4,description:`Home of Michelangelo's David, far more powerful in person than in any photo, plus his unfinished 'Prisoners' straining out of the marble.`,tip:`Closed Mondays. Without a reservation the queue can run 1–2 hours.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Galleria dell'Accademia`},{id:`ponte-vecchio`,name:`Ponte Vecchio`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`bridge`,`free`,`sunset`,`jewellery`],area:`Signoria`,lat:43.768,lng:11.2531,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Florence's medieval bridge, lined with goldsmiths' shops and topped by the Vasari Corridor, is most beautiful glowing at sunset.`,tip:`For the best photo of the bridge, stand on the neighbouring Ponte Santa Trinita.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Ponte Vecchio`},{id:`palazzo-vecchio`,name:`Piazza della Signoria & Palazzo Vecchio`,category:`culture`,tags:[`piazza`,`sculpture`,`history`,`tower`],area:`Signoria`,lat:43.7693,lng:11.2563,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:19,rating:4,description:`Florence's civic heart: an open-air sculpture gallery in the Loggia dei Lanzi and the fortress-like town hall with its lavish Hall of the Five Hundred.`,tip:`The piazza and Loggia are free; the palace museum is open late on most evenings except Thursday.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Palazzo Vecchio`},{id:`piazzale-michelangelo`,name:`Piazzale Michelangelo`,category:`nature`,tags:[`viewpoint`,`sunset`,`free`,`panorama`],area:`San Niccolò`,lat:43.7629,lng:11.2651,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The postcard panorama of Florence — the Duomo, Palazzo Vecchio and the Arno's bridges — from a hilltop terrace.`,tip:`Walk up through the Rose Garden from San Niccolò, then continue to San Miniato for vespers.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Piazzale Michelangelo`},{id:`san-miniato`,name:`San Miniato al Monte`,category:`culture`,tags:[`church`,`free`,`viewpoint`,`gregorian-chant`,`sunset`],area:`San Niccolò`,lat:43.7594,lng:11.2649,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`One of Tuscany's finest Romanesque churches, crowning the hill above Piazzale Michelangelo with an even quieter view.`,tip:`The Olivetan monks sing Gregorian chant at vespers in the early evening — check the current time at the door.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`San Miniato al Monte`},{id:`boboli-gardens`,name:`Boboli Gardens`,localName:`Giardino di Boboli`,category:`nature`,tags:[`garden`,`renaissance`,`kids`],area:`Oltrarno`,lat:43.7625,lng:11.248,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:4,description:`The Medici's terraced hillside garden behind Palazzo Pitti, full of grottoes, fountains, cypress avenues and city views.`,tip:`Some first Sundays of the month are free; the garden closes on the first and last Monday of each month.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Boboli Gardens`},{id:`palazzo-pitti`,name:`Pitti Palace`,localName:`Palazzo Pitti`,category:`museum`,tags:[`palace`,`art`,`rainy-day`],area:`Oltrarno`,lat:43.7651,lng:11.25,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:18,rating:3,description:`The vast Medici palace holds the Palatine Gallery's Raphaels and Titians in gilded royal apartments.`,tip:`Closed Mondays. A combined ticket with Boboli and the Uffizi saves money if you plan all three.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Palazzo Pitti`},{id:`mercato-centrale`,name:`Mercato Centrale`,category:`food`,tags:[`market`,`food-hall`,`lampredotto`,`rainy-day`],area:`San Lorenzo`,lat:43.7764,lng:11.2534,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:14,rating:4,description:`A 19th-century iron-and-glass market: produce stalls downstairs, a lively food hall of pasta, pizza and truffle counters upstairs.`,tip:`Head to Da Nerbone on the ground floor for a classic boiled-beef or lampredotto sandwich (lunchtime only).`,indoor:!0},{id:`santa-croce`,name:`Basilica di Santa Croce`,category:`culture`,tags:[`church`,`tombs`,`giotto`,`rainy-day`],area:`Santa Croce`,lat:43.7686,lng:11.2623,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:11,rating:4,description:`The great Franciscan basilica is the resting place of Michelangelo, Galileo and Machiavelli, with frescoes by Giotto.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Basilica of Santa Croce, Florence`},{id:`scuola-del-cuoio`,name:`Scuola del Cuoio Leather School`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`leather`,`craft`,`free`,`rainy-day`],area:`Santa Croce`,lat:43.7683,lng:11.2626,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A leather workshop founded after WWII in the former Santa Croce dormitory; watch artisans at work and buy genuinely Florentine goods.`,tip:`Free to browse — a trustworthy alternative to the hit-and-miss street stalls around San Lorenzo.`,indoor:!0},{id:`bargello`,name:`Bargello National Museum`,localName:`Museo Nazionale del Bargello`,category:`museum`,tags:[`sculpture`,`donatello`,`rainy-day`,`uncrowded`],area:`Signoria`,lat:43.7704,lng:11.2582,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:4,description:`A medieval prison turned sculpture museum, with Donatello's bronze David and early Michelangelos — usually blissfully uncrowded.`,tip:`Hours are shorter than other museums; check before you go, and note it closes on some Sundays and Mondays.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Bargello`},{id:`museo-galileo`,name:`Museo Galileo`,category:`family`,tags:[`science`,`kids`,`rainy-day`],area:`Signoria`,lat:43.7677,lng:11.256,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:14,rating:3,description:`Galileo's own telescopes (and, curiously, his finger) among beautiful globes, clocks and scientific instruments by the Arno.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Museo Galileo`},{id:`santo-spirito`,name:`Piazza Santo Spirito`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`bars`,`aperitivo`,`local`,`free`],area:`Oltrarno`,lat:43.7665,lng:11.2479,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The Oltrarno's bohemian living room: locals spill out of wine bars onto the church steps for aperitivo and late-night chatter.`,tip:`Combine with dinner in the surrounding Oltrarno trattorias; book ahead on weekends.`,indoor:!1},{id:`sant-ambrogio-market`,name:`Sant'Ambrogio Market`,localName:`Mercato di Sant'Ambrogio`,category:`food`,tags:[`market`,`local`,`lunch`],area:`Santa Croce`,lat:43.7697,lng:11.2659,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:3,description:`A down-to-earth neighbourhood market where Florentines actually shop, with a cheap, cheerful trattoria (Da Rocco) inside.`,tip:`Closed Sundays; mornings are liveliest.`,indoor:!0},{id:`fiesole`,name:`Fiesole`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`hill-town`,`viewpoint`,`roman-theatre`,`half-day`],area:`Fiesole`,lat:43.8064,lng:11.2924,durationHours:3.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:14,rating:3,description:`A cool hilltop village with Etruscan walls, a Roman theatre and a sweeping view of Florence in the valley below.`,tip:`Bus 7 from San Marco takes about 25 minutes. Stay for sunset, then dinner on the piazza.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Fiesole`},{id:`chianti-wine-tour`,name:`Chianti Wine Country Day Trip`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`day-trip`,`wine`,`countryside`,`tasting`],area:`Chianti`,lat:43.5843,lng:11.3172,durationHours:7,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:120,rating:4,description:`Rolling vineyards, castles and cypress-lined roads between Florence and Siena, with Chianti Classico tastings at family estates around Greve.`,tip:`Join a small-group tour or hire a driver so nobody has to drive after tastings.`,indoor:!1},{id:`pisa-day-trip`,name:`Pisa Day Trip (Leaning Tower)`,localName:`Piazza dei Miracoli`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`day-trip`,`iconic`,`unesco`,`kids`],area:`Pisa`,lat:43.723,lng:10.3966,durationHours:5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:45,rating:4,description:`The leaning bell tower, cathedral and baptistery stand on a brilliant green lawn — about an hour by train from Florence.`,tip:`Book a timed tower climb online (children under 8 can't climb). Train fare plus tower is roughly €40.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Piazza dei Miracoli`},{id:`medici-chapels`,name:`Medici Chapels`,localName:`Cappelle Medicee`,category:`museum`,tags:[`michelangelo`,`sculpture`,`tombs`,`rainy-day`],area:`San Lorenzo`,lat:43.7752,lng:11.2533,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:14,rating:4,description:`The Medici mausoleum behind San Lorenzo: the marble-inlaid Chapel of the Princes and Michelangelo's New Sacristy with his brooding figures of Night and Day.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Medici Chapel`},{id:`santa-maria-novella`,name:`Basilica of Santa Maria Novella`,localName:`Santa Maria Novella`,category:`culture`,tags:[`church`,`frescoes`,`masaccio`,`rainy-day`],area:`Santa Maria Novella`,lat:43.7746,lng:11.2493,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:9,rating:4,description:`Alberti's marble façade fronts a Dominican church packed with masterpieces, including Masaccio's pioneering Holy Trinity and Ghirlandaio's frescoed choir chapel.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Santa Maria Novella`},{id:`officina-profumo-farmaceutica`,name:`Officina Profumo-Farmaceutica di Santa Maria Novella`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`perfume`,`historic-shop`,`free`,`rainy-day`],area:`Santa Maria Novella`,lat:43.7737,lng:11.2478,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`One of the world's oldest pharmacies, founded by Dominican friars, selling perfumes, soaps and herbal elixirs in frescoed, incense-scented halls.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Officina Profumo-Farmaceutica di Santa Maria Novella`},{id:`san-marco-museum`,name:`Museum of San Marco`,localName:`Museo di San Marco`,category:`museum`,tags:[`fra-angelico`,`frescoes`,`uncrowded`,`rainy-day`],area:`San Marco`,lat:43.7782,lng:11.2587,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:13,rating:4,description:`A serene Dominican convent where Fra Angelico painted a gentle fresco in every friar's cell, with his celebrated Annunciation at the top of the stairs.`,tip:`Opening hours are short and vary by day — check before you go.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Museo Nazionale di San Marco`},{id:`palazzo-medici-riccardi`,name:`Palazzo Medici Riccardi`,category:`museum`,tags:[`palace`,`frescoes`,`medici`,`rainy-day`],area:`San Lorenzo`,lat:43.7752,lng:11.256,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:18,rating:3,description:`The Medici's first family palace, best known for the tiny Magi Chapel, where Benozzo Gozzoli's procession frescoes shimmer with gold and Medici portraits.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Palazzo Medici Riccardi`},{id:`gelateria-vivoli`,name:`Gelateria Vivoli`,category:`food`,tags:[`gelato`,`historic`,`sweet`],area:`Santa Croce`,lat:43.7697,lng:11.2597,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:5,rating:4,description:`One of Florence's oldest gelaterias, tucked down a lane near Santa Croce, famous for its rice gelato and espresso-drowned affogato.`,indoor:!0},{id:`san-niccolo-evening`,name:`San Niccolò Evening`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`neighbourhood`,`wine-bars`,`aperitivo`,`local`],area:`San Niccolò`,lat:43.7643,lng:11.2597,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A villagey strip at the foot of the hill below Piazzale Michelangelo, where wine bars and trattorias spill onto Via di San Niccolò beside a medieval city gate.`,tip:`Watch the sunset from Piazzale Michelangelo first, then walk down the steps for dinner here.`,indoor:!1},{id:`bardini-garden`,name:`Bardini Garden`,localName:`Giardino Bardini`,category:`nature`,tags:[`garden`,`viewpoint`,`wisteria`,`uncrowded`],area:`San Niccolò`,lat:43.7652,lng:11.2576,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:4,description:`A quieter alternative to Boboli: terraced hillside gardens with a baroque staircase, a wisteria tunnel that blooms in late April and superb views over the rooftops.`,indoor:!1},{id:`brancacci-chapel`,name:`Brancacci Chapel`,localName:`Cappella Brancacci`,category:`museum`,tags:[`frescoes`,`masaccio`,`renaissance`,`rainy-day`],area:`Oltrarno`,lat:43.7679,lng:11.2437,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:4,description:`Masaccio's frescoes in this chapel of Santa Maria del Carmine — including the anguished Expulsion from Eden — taught a generation of Renaissance painters.`,tip:`Entry is in small timed groups; reserve ahead, especially at weekends.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Brancacci Chapel`},{id:`opera-di-firenze`,name:`Opera di Firenze`,localName:`Teatro del Maggio Musicale Fiorentino`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`opera`,`concerts`,`classical`,`rainy-day`],area:`Cascine`,lat:43.777,lng:11.2375,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:45,rating:3,description:`Florence's modern opera house, home of the Maggio Musicale festival, stages opera, ballet and symphony concerts beside the Cascine park.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Teatro del Maggio Musicale Fiorentino`},{id:`cascine-park`,name:`Cascine Park`,localName:`Parco delle Cascine`,category:`nature`,tags:[`park`,`free`,`running`,`market`,`kids`],area:`Cascine`,lat:43.7817,lng:11.229,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The Medici's former dairy estate is now Florence's largest park, a long green strip along the Arno with plane-tree avenues, playgrounds and cycle paths.`,tip:`A huge open-air market fills the main avenue every Tuesday morning.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Parco delle Cascine`},{id:`stibbert-museum`,name:`Stibbert Museum`,localName:`Museo Stibbert`,category:`family`,tags:[`armour`,`kids`,`quirky`,`rainy-day`],area:`Montughi`,lat:43.7902,lng:11.2499,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:3,description:`An eccentric Anglo-Italian collector's hillside villa crammed with armour — including a cavalcade of mounted knights and samurai — that delights kids and adults alike.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Museo Stibbert`},{id:`siena-day-trip`,name:`Siena Day Trip`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`day-trip`,`medieval`,`unesco`,`piazza`],area:`Siena`,lat:43.3184,lng:11.3316,durationHours:8,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:35,rating:4,description:`Florence's Gothic rival, with the shell-shaped Piazza del Campo, a striped cathedral with an inlaid marble floor and a maze of steep brick lanes.`,tip:`Express buses from Florence take about 75 minutes and drop you closer to the centre than the train.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Siena`},{id:`via-tornabuoni`,name:`Via de' Tornabuoni`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`fashion`,`luxury`,`boutiques`,`free`],area:`Tornabuoni`,lat:43.7714,lng:11.251,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Florence's grandest shopping street, where Renaissance palaces house Gucci, Ferragamo and the rest of Italian high fashion.`,tip:`Ferragamo's flagship in Palazzo Spini Feroni has a shoe museum downstairs.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Via de' Tornabuoni`},{id:`piazza-della-repubblica`,name:`Piazza della Repubblica`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`piazza`,`carousel`,`historic-cafe`,`rooftop`,`free`],area:`Duomo`,lat:43.7714,lng:11.254,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A grand 19th-century square on the site of the Roman forum, with an antique carousel, historic cafés like Gilli and a rooftop terrace atop La Rinascente.`,tip:`The Rinascente rooftop café has close-up Duomo views — lovely at aperitivo hour.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Piazza della Repubblica, Florence`},{id:`santo-spirito-basilica`,name:`Basilica of Santo Spirito`,localName:`Basilica di Santo Spirito`,category:`culture`,tags:[`church`,`brunelleschi`,`michelangelo`,`rainy-day`],area:`Oltrarno`,lat:43.7669,lng:11.2479,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:2,rating:3,description:`Brunelleschi's last church, a study in perfect proportion behind a plain façade, with a wooden crucifix carved by a teenage Michelangelo in the sacristy.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Santo Spirito, Florence`},{id:`antico-vinaio`,name:`All'Antico Vinaio`,category:`food`,tags:[`sandwich`,`street-food`,`lunch`,`queue`],area:`Signoria`,lat:43.7684,lng:11.2571,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:4,description:`Florence's cult schiacciata shop on Via dei Neri, slicing huge focaccia sandwiches loaded with mortadella, pistachio cream and truffle.`,tip:`The queue moves fast, and several branches along Via dei Neri share the load.`,indoor:!1}],foods:[{name:`Florentine T-bone Steak`,localName:`Bistecca alla Fiorentina`,description:`A thick, chargrilled T-bone of Chianina beef served very rare and priced by the kilo — share one.`},{name:`Lampredotto Sandwich`,localName:`Panino col Lampredotto`,description:`Tripe slow-cooked in broth, piled into a bun with salsa verde; Florence's street-food classic.`},{name:`Ribollita`,description:`A thick 'reboiled' Tuscan soup of bread, cannellini beans and cavolo nero.`},{name:`Pappa al Pomodoro`,description:`Bread and ripe tomato simmered into a comforting porridge with basil and olive oil.`},{name:`Schiacciata Sandwich`,localName:`Schiacciata`,description:`Salty, oily Tuscan flatbread stuffed with salumi, pecorino and truffle cream — try All'Antico Vinaio or a local alimentari.`},{name:`Cantucci with Vin Santo`,localName:`Cantucci e Vin Santo`,description:`Crunchy almond biscotti dunked in amber dessert wine to end a meal.`}]},{id:`venice`,name:`Venice`,localName:`Venezia`,lat:45.4408,lng:12.3155,timezone:`Europe/Rome`,tagline:`A floating city of canals, palaces and cicchetti`,description:`Built on more than a hundred islands, car-free Venice is a maze of canals, bridges and crumbling palazzi. Lose yourself in the backstreets, then rejoin the crowds for Byzantine mosaics and Grand Canal views.`,idealDays:[2,3],places:[{id:`st-marks-basilica`,name:`St. Mark's Basilica`,localName:`Basilica di San Marco`,category:`culture`,tags:[`iconic`,`church`,`mosaics`,`rainy-day`],area:`San Marco`,lat:45.4345,lng:12.3397,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:8,rating:5,description:`A glittering Byzantine basilica whose domes are lined with over 8,000 square metres of gold mosaics.`,tip:`Book a timed entry online to skip the line. Shoulders and knees must be covered and large bags aren't allowed. The Pala d'Oro and terrace cost extra.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`St Mark's Basilica`},{id:`doges-palace`,name:`Doge's Palace`,localName:`Palazzo Ducale`,category:`museum`,tags:[`iconic`,`palace`,`history`,`rainy-day`],area:`San Marco`,lat:45.4337,lng:12.3404,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:35,rating:5,description:`The pink-and-white Gothic seat of the Venetian Republic, with Tintoretto's vast Paradise and a walk across the Bridge of Sighs into the prisons.`,tip:`The 'Secret Itineraries' guided tour reveals hidden offices and Casanova's cell — book well ahead.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Doge's Palace`},{id:`piazza-san-marco-caffe-florian`,name:`Piazza San Marco & Caffè Florian`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`iconic`,`piazza`,`live-music`,`historic-cafe`,`night-view`],area:`San Marco`,lat:45.4339,lng:12.3381,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:4,description:`Napoleon's 'drawing room of Europe' is magical at night, when the crowds thin and café orchestras play under the arcades. Florian has served coffee here since 1720.`,tip:`A music surcharge is added when the orchestra plays; standing on the piazza and listening is free.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Piazza San Marco`},{id:`grand-canal-vaporetto`,name:`Grand Canal by Vaporetto Line 1`,localName:`Canal Grande`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`boat`,`palaces`,`sightseeing`],area:`Cannaregio`,lat:45.4411,lng:12.3212,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:11,rating:4,description:`The slow Line 1 water bus glides the full length of the Grand Canal past some 170 palaces — the cheapest grand tour in Italy.`,tip:`Board at Ferrovia and grab a seat at the front or back. A 24–72 hour pass beats single €9.50 tickets if you'll ride more than twice.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Grand Canal (Venice)`},{id:`rialto-bridge`,name:`Rialto Bridge`,localName:`Ponte di Rialto`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`bridge`,`free`,`photo-spot`],area:`San Polo`,lat:45.438,lng:12.3359,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The 16th-century stone bridge arching over the Grand Canal, lined with shops and crowds in equal measure.`,tip:`For the view without the crush, try the rooftop terrace of the Fondaco dei Tedeschi (free, booking required) next door.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Rialto Bridge`},{id:`rialto-market`,name:`Rialto Market`,localName:`Mercato di Rialto`,category:`food`,tags:[`market`,`seafood`,`local`,`free`],area:`San Polo`,lat:45.4398,lng:12.334,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Venice's centuries-old produce and fish market, piled with lagoon crabs, artichokes and gleaming fish under a Gothic loggia.`,tip:`Come before 10am. The fish market (Pescheria) is closed Sundays and Mondays.`,indoor:!1},{id:`cicchetti-crawl`,name:`Cicchetti Bar Crawl`,localName:`Giro di bàcari`,category:`food`,tags:[`bacari`,`wine`,`spritz`,`local`],area:`San Polo`,lat:45.4389,lng:12.3346,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:4,description:`Hop between bàcari like Cantina Do Mori (since 1462) and All'Arco for small bites on bread and an 'ombra' of wine, standing at the counter like a Venetian.`,tip:`Many bàcari close early (around 8pm) and on Sundays — start around 6pm.`,indoor:!0},{id:`gallerie-accademia`,name:`Gallerie dell'Accademia`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`titian`,`bellini`,`rainy-day`],area:`Dorsoduro`,lat:45.4312,lng:12.3282,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:17,rating:4,description:`The definitive collection of Venetian painting, from Bellini and Giorgione to Titian, Tintoretto and Veronese.`,tip:`Mondays it closes early (around 2pm).`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Gallerie dell'Accademia`},{id:`peggy-guggenheim`,name:`Peggy Guggenheim Collection`,category:`museum`,tags:[`modern-art`,`canal-view`,`rainy-day`],area:`Dorsoduro`,lat:45.4307,lng:12.3316,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:21,rating:4,description:`Pollock, Picasso, Magritte and Calder in the heiress's unfinished palazzo on the Grand Canal, with a lovely sculpture garden.`,tip:`Closed Tuesdays. Booking online is recommended.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Peggy Guggenheim Collection`},{id:`santa-maria-della-salute`,name:`Basilica di Santa Maria della Salute`,category:`culture`,tags:[`church`,`baroque`,`free`,`rainy-day`],area:`Dorsoduro`,lat:45.4308,lng:12.3346,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The great white domed church at the mouth of the Grand Canal, built in thanks for the end of the 1630 plague.`,tip:`Entry to the church is free; the sacristy with its Titians and Tintoretto costs a few euros.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Santa Maria della Salute`},{id:`scuola-grande-san-rocco`,name:`Scuola Grande di San Rocco`,category:`museum`,tags:[`tintoretto`,`art`,`rainy-day`,`uncrowded`],area:`San Polo`,lat:45.4365,lng:12.3264,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:4,description:`A confraternity hall smothered floor to ceiling in more than 60 Tintoretto canvases — often called Venice's Sistine Chapel.`,tip:`Pick up one of the free hand mirrors to study the ceiling without straining your neck.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Scuola Grande di San Rocco`},{id:`gondola-ride`,name:`Gondola Ride`,localName:`Giro in gondola`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`iconic`,`boat`,`romantic`,`canals`],area:`San Marco`,lat:45.435,lng:12.337,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:45,rating:4,description:`A 30-minute glide through quiet back canals with a striped-shirted gondolier — touristy, yes, but unforgettable.`,tip:`Official fares are about €90 by day and €110 after 7pm per boat (up to 5 people); split it. For €2 you can cross the Grand Canal standing in a traghetto gondola.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Gondola`},{id:`burano`,name:`Burano`,category:`family`,tags:[`island`,`colourful`,`lace`,`half-day`,`kids`],area:`Burano`,lat:45.4853,lng:12.417,durationHours:3.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:11,rating:4,description:`A lagoon fishing village of rainbow-painted houses, lace shops and canal-side seafood lunches.`,tip:`Take vaporetto 12 from Fondamente Nove (about 40 minutes); pair it with Murano on a day pass.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Burano`},{id:`murano-glass`,name:`Murano Glass Museum`,localName:`Museo del Vetro`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`island`,`glass`,`craft`,`rainy-day`],area:`Murano`,lat:45.4558,lng:12.3528,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:3,description:`The island of glassmakers since 1291: watch a furnace demonstration, see a millennium of glass in the museum, and shop for the real thing.`,tip:`Look for the 'Vetro Artistico Murano' trademark to avoid imported fakes.`,indoor:!0},{id:`san-giorgio-maggiore`,name:`San Giorgio Maggiore Bell Tower`,localName:`Campanile di San Giorgio Maggiore`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`viewpoint`,`sunset`,`palladio`,`uncrowded`],area:`San Giorgio`,lat:45.4292,lng:12.3433,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:4,description:`Palladio's island church has a lift up its campanile to the best view of St. Mark's — with a fraction of the queue.`,tip:`Vaporetto 2 stops right outside, one hop from San Zaccaria.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`San Giorgio Maggiore`},{id:`cannaregio-misericordia`,name:`Fondamenta della Misericordia`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`canal-side`,`bars`,`local`,`aperitivo`,`free`],area:`Cannaregio`,lat:45.4448,lng:12.3315,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Cannaregio's long canal-side quays (Misericordia and Ormesini) are where young Venetians gather for spritz and cicchetti after dark.`,indoor:!1},{id:`jewish-ghetto`,name:`Jewish Ghetto`,localName:`Ghetto Ebraico`,category:`culture`,tags:[`history`,`neighbourhood`,`free`],area:`Cannaregio`,lat:45.4447,lng:12.3263,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The world's first ghetto (1516), with unusually tall buildings and hidden synagogues around the Campo del Ghetto Nuovo.`,tip:`Synagogue tours are run by the Jewish community; times vary and there are none on Saturdays and Jewish holidays.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Venetian Ghetto`},{id:`libreria-acqua-alta`,name:`Libreria Acqua Alta`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`bookshop`,`quirky`,`free`,`rainy-day`],area:`Castello`,lat:45.438,lng:12.3426,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A gloriously chaotic bookshop where books are stacked in bathtubs and a gondola to survive the high tides, with a staircase made of old volumes.`,tip:`Arrive at opening to avoid queues; resident cats included.`,indoor:!0},{id:`lido-beach`,name:`Lido di Venezia Beach`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`beach`,`island`,`summer`,`kids`],area:`Lido`,lat:45.4095,lng:12.372,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:11,rating:3,description:`Venice's long Adriatic barrier island has sandy beaches, Art Nouveau villas and — unusually for Venice — bicycles and cars.`,tip:`Free public beach sections sit beside paid lidos with umbrellas and loungers; best June–September.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Lido di Venezia`},{id:`torcello`,name:`Torcello`,category:`culture`,tags:[`island`,`mosaics`,`byzantine`,`half-day`,`uncrowded`],area:`Torcello`,lat:45.4975,lng:12.4183,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:14,rating:4,description:`The lagoon's first settlement, now home to only a handful of residents, with a thousand-year-old cathedral whose Last Judgment mosaic rivals St. Mark's.`,tip:`A short ferry hop from Burano — combine both in one trip, and climb the bell tower for marshland views.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Torcello`},{id:`ca-doro`,name:`Ca' d'Oro`,localName:`Galleria Giorgio Franchetti alla Ca' d'Oro`,category:`museum`,tags:[`palace`,`gothic`,`art`,`canal-view`,`rainy-day`],area:`Cannaregio`,lat:45.4406,lng:12.3343,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:13,rating:3,description:`The most ornate Gothic palace on the Grand Canal, its lacy marble façade once gilded, now a gallery holding Mantegna's St Sebastian and a loggia over the water.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Ca' d'Oro`},{id:`ca-rezzonico`,name:`Ca' Rezzonico`,category:`museum`,tags:[`palace`,`18th-century`,`art`,`rainy-day`],area:`Dorsoduro`,lat:45.4338,lng:12.3267,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:16,rating:4,description:`A grand Baroque palazzo recreating 18th-century Venetian life, with Tiepolo ceilings, Murano chandeliers and Longhi's gossipy scenes of society.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Ca' Rezzonico`},{id:`frari`,name:`Basilica dei Frari`,localName:`Santa Maria Gloriosa dei Frari`,category:`culture`,tags:[`church`,`titian`,`art`,`rainy-day`],area:`San Polo`,lat:45.4369,lng:12.3263,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:7,rating:4,description:`A soaring brick Gothic church holding Titian's blazing Assumption above the high altar, the painter's own tomb and Canova's pyramid monument.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Santa Maria Gloriosa dei Frari`},{id:`st-marks-campanile`,name:`St. Mark's Campanile`,localName:`Campanile di San Marco`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`viewpoint`,`iconic`,`lift`],area:`San Marco`,lat:45.434,lng:12.339,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:13,rating:4,description:`A lift whisks you up the 99-metre bell tower for a bird's-eye view of St. Mark's domes, the lagoon and, on clear days, the Alps.`,tip:`It collapsed in 1902 and was rebuilt 'as it was, where it was'; cover your ears if you're up top when the bells ring the hour.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`St Mark's Campanile`},{id:`la-fenice`,name:`Teatro La Fenice`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`opera`,`theatre`,`classical`,`rainy-day`],area:`San Marco`,lat:45.4337,lng:12.3336,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:90,rating:4,description:`Venice's jewel-box opera house, risen from the ashes more than once, stages opera and concerts in a gilded horseshoe auditorium.`,tip:`If you can't catch a performance, self-guided audio tours of the theatre run during the day.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`La Fenice`},{id:`venice-biennale`,name:`Venice Biennale (Giardini & Arsenale)`,localName:`La Biennale di Venezia`,category:`museum`,tags:[`contemporary-art`,`architecture`,`seasonal`],area:`Castello`,lat:45.4291,lng:12.3575,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:35,rating:4,description:`The world's most famous exhibition alternates yearly between art and architecture, filling national pavilions in the Giardini and the vast Arsenale shipyards.`,tip:`Runs roughly May to November; one ticket covers both venues, which deserve a full day.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Venice Biennale`},{id:`arsenale`,name:`Venetian Arsenal`,localName:`Arsenale di Venezia`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`history`,`maritime`,`free`,`walk`],area:`Castello`,lat:45.4348,lng:12.3503,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The Republic's medieval shipyard could build a galley in a day; its fortified Renaissance land gate, guarded by stone lions, is free to admire from the canal-side.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Venetian Arsenal`},{id:`scala-contarini-del-bovolo`,name:`Scala Contarini del Bovolo`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`staircase`,`viewpoint`,`hidden-gem`,`photo-spot`],area:`San Marco`,lat:45.4349,lng:12.333,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:3,description:`A slender external spiral staircase of white arches winding up a hidden palazzo courtyard, with rooftop views at the top.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Palazzo Contarini del Bovolo`},{id:`zattere`,name:`Zattere Promenade`,category:`relaxation`,tags:[`waterfront`,`sunset`,`free`,`gelato`],area:`Dorsoduro`,lat:45.4296,lng:12.3262,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A long, sunny quay along the wide Giudecca Canal where Venetians stroll, sit on café pontoons over the water and watch the evening light fade.`,tip:`Order a gianduiotto — a slab of hazelnut-chocolate gelato drowned in whipped cream — at Gelateria Nico.`,indoor:!1},{id:`campo-santa-margherita`,name:`Campo Santa Margherita`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`bars`,`students`,`aperitivo`,`local`,`free`],area:`Dorsoduro`,lat:45.4343,lng:12.3237,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A long, lively square in student Dorsoduro, where cheap spritz bars and outdoor tables keep the atmosphere authentically Venetian late into the night.`,indoor:!1},{id:`squero-san-trovaso`,name:`Squero di San Trovaso`,category:`culture`,tags:[`gondola`,`craft`,`free`,`photo-spot`],area:`Dorsoduro`,lat:45.431,lng:12.3264,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`One of Venice's last working gondola boatyards, a timber, Alpine-style shed where craftsmen build and repair gondolas by hand.`,tip:`It's a working yard, not an attraction — watch from the opposite side of the canal.`,indoor:!1},{id:`natural-history-museum`,name:`Natural History Museum of Venice`,localName:`Museo di Storia Naturale di Venezia`,category:`family`,tags:[`dinosaurs`,`kids`,`rainy-day`],area:`Santa Croce`,lat:45.4413,lng:12.3303,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:3,description:`Housed in the Grand Canal's Fondaco dei Turchi, with a huge Ouranosaurus skeleton, cabinets of curiosities and explorers' trophies that kids love.`,indoor:!0},{id:`scrovegni-chapel`,name:`Scrovegni Chapel, Padua`,localName:`Cappella degli Scrovegni`,category:`museum`,tags:[`day-trip`,`giotto`,`frescoes`,`unesco`],area:`Padua`,lat:45.4114,lng:11.8796,durationHours:5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:4,description:`Giotto's ultramarine-blue fresco cycle, a turning point in Western art, fills this small chapel in Padua, about 30 minutes from Venice by train.`,tip:`Visits are strictly timed short slots after a stint in a climate-control room — book well ahead.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Scrovegni Chapel`},{id:`verona-day-trip`,name:`Verona Day Trip`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`day-trip`,`roman-arena`,`romeo-and-juliet`,`unesco`],area:`Verona`,lat:45.439,lng:10.9944,durationHours:8,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:40,rating:4,description:`Romeo and Juliet's city has a Roman amphitheatre still used for summer opera, pastel piazzas and a looping river, about 70 minutes away by fast train.`,tip:`In summer, stay for an evening opera at the Arena and catch a late train back.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Verona`},{id:`pasticceria-tonolo`,name:`Pasticceria Tonolo`,category:`food`,tags:[`pastries`,`coffee`,`breakfast`,`local`],area:`Dorsoduro`,lat:45.4358,lng:12.3248,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:6,rating:4,description:`A tiny, perpetually busy pastry shop where Venetians stand at the counter for espresso and cream-filled pastries — and frittelle at Carnival time.`,indoor:!0},{id:`interpreti-veneziani`,name:`Interpreti Veneziani Concert`,localName:`Chiesa di San Vidal`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`classical`,`concert`,`vivaldi`,`rainy-day`],area:`San Marco`,lat:45.4322,lng:12.3296,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:35,rating:4,description:`A first-rate baroque string ensemble plays Vivaldi and friends in the deconsecrated church of San Vidal, by the Accademia bridge.`,indoor:!0}],foods:[{name:`Sweet-and-Sour Sardines`,localName:`Sarde in Saor`,description:`Fried sardines marinated with onions, vinegar, pine nuts and raisins — an old sailors' preserve.`},{name:`Creamed Salt Cod`,localName:`Baccalà Mantecato`,description:`Whipped dried cod spread on bread or grilled polenta, the king of cicchetti.`},{name:`Squid-Ink Risotto`,localName:`Risotto al Nero di Seppia`,description:`Jet-black risotto made with cuttlefish and its ink, rich with the taste of the lagoon.`},{name:`Bigoli in Salsa`,description:`Thick wholewheat noodles in a slow-cooked sauce of onions and anchovies.`},{name:`Venetian-Style Liver`,localName:`Fegato alla Veneziana`,description:`Thin slices of calf's liver with sweet, slow-cooked onions, served with polenta.`},{name:`Tramezzino`,description:`Soft crustless triangle sandwiches stuffed generously with tuna, egg or prawns — a Venetian bar staple.`}]},{id:`milan`,name:`Milan`,localName:`Milano`,lat:45.46417,lng:9.19,timezone:`Europe/Rome`,tagline:`Gothic spires, Leonardo and the art of the aperitivo`,description:`Italy's capital of fashion, design and finance hides serious treasures behind its business-like face: a marble Gothic cathedral you can walk across, Leonardo's Last Supper and canal-side bars that fill at aperitivo hour. Lake Como and Bergamo are an easy train ride away.`,idealDays:[2,4],places:[{id:`milan-cathedral`,name:`Milan Cathedral & Rooftop Terraces`,localName:`Duomo di Milano`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`architecture`,`gothic`,`viewpoint`,`rooftop`],area:`Duomo`,lat:45.46417,lng:9.19139,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:5,description:`A forest of white marble spires and statues that took six centuries to finish. Inside, vast stained-glass windows; above, rooftop terraces where you walk among the pinnacles beneath the golden Madonnina.`,tip:`Buy a combined ticket online with a timed slot; the lift to the terraces costs a little more than the stairs but saves a long climb. Shoulders and knees must be covered.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Milan Cathedral`},{id:`galleria-vittorio-emanuele`,name:`Galleria Vittorio Emanuele II`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`architecture`,`arcade`,`free`,`shopping`],area:`Duomo`,lat:45.46556,lng:9.19,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`Milan's glass-domed 19th-century shopping arcade links the Duomo to La Scala, lined with mosaics, luxury boutiques and historic cafes.`,tip:`Locals spin on their heel on the bull mosaic's worn spot for luck. It is at its most atmospheric when lit up after dark.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Galleria Vittorio Emanuele II`},{id:`last-supper`,name:`Leonardo's Last Supper`,localName:`Cenacolo Vinciano`,category:`museum`,tags:[`iconic`,`leonardo`,`art`,`fresco`,`rainy-day`],area:`Magenta`,lat:45.46667,lng:9.17083,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:18,rating:5,description:`Leonardo da Vinci's fragile masterpiece covers a wall of the refectory beside Santa Maria delle Grazie. Visits are limited to about 15 minutes in small groups.`,tip:`Tickets sell out weeks or months ahead; they are released in batches on the official site. Closed Mondays.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`The Last Supper (Leonardo)`},{id:`sforza-castle`,name:`Sforza Castle`,localName:`Castello Sforzesco`,category:`museum`,tags:[`castle`,`history`,`michelangelo`,`rainy-day`],area:`Castello`,lat:45.47,lng:9.17861,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:4,description:`The Sforza dukes' brick fortress houses a cluster of civic museums, including Michelangelo's last, unfinished sculpture, the Rondanini Pieta, and a ceiling painted by Leonardo.`,tip:`The courtyards are free to wander; museums are closed Mondays.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Sforza Castle`},{id:`parco-sempione`,name:`Parco Sempione`,category:`nature`,tags:[`park`,`free`,`picnic`,`family`],area:`Castello`,lat:45.473,lng:9.17697,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Milan's big central park stretches from the back of Sforza Castle to the Arch of Peace, with lawns, a pond, Torre Branca and the Triennale design museum.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Parco Sempione`},{id:`arco-della-pace`,name:`Arch of Peace`,localName:`Arco della Pace`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`monument`,`neoclassical`,`free`,`sunset`],area:`Sempione`,lat:45.47569,lng:9.17243,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A Napoleonic triumphal arch at the end of Parco Sempione, crowned by a bronze chariot. The surrounding Corso Sempione is lined with aperitivo bars.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Porta Sempione`},{id:`pinacoteca-di-brera`,name:`Pinacoteca di Brera`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`renaissance`,`caravaggio`,`rainy-day`],area:`Brera`,lat:45.47194,lng:9.18806,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:5,description:`Milan's great picture gallery, inside a 17th-century palazzo, holds Mantegna's Lamentation over the Dead Christ, Raphael's Marriage of the Virgin and Caravaggio's Supper at Emmaus.`,tip:`Closed Mondays. Look into the glass-walled restoration lab where conservators work on paintings.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Pinacoteca di Brera`},{id:`brera-district`,name:`Brera Quarter`,category:`culture`,tags:[`neighbourhood`,`cobblestones`,`galleries`,`free`,`aperitivo`],area:`Brera`,lat:45.47139,lng:9.185,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Milan's old artists' quarter is a web of cobbled lanes with galleries, design shops, wine bars and pavement tables, liveliest around Via Fiori Chiari at aperitivo hour.`,tip:`Duck into the Orto Botanico di Brera, a small free botanic garden behind the Pinacoteca.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Brera, Milan`},{id:`la-scala`,name:`Teatro alla Scala`,localName:`La Scala`,category:`culture`,tags:[`opera`,`ballet`,`iconic`,`music`,`rainy-day`],area:`Duomo`,lat:45.4675,lng:9.18917,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:90,rating:4,description:`The world's most famous opera house, where Verdi and Puccini premiered works. An evening performance under the red-and-gold tiers is unforgettable; the theatre museum offers a daytime peek.`,tip:`Cheap upper-gallery seats and same-day tickets exist. If no performance fits, the museum (about 15 euros) lets you look into the auditorium from a box.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`La Scala`},{id:`navigli`,name:`Navigli Canals & Darsena`,localName:`Navigli`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`canals`,`aperitivo`,`bars`,`sunset`,`vintage`],area:`Navigli`,lat:45.45291,lng:9.17857,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:14,rating:4,description:`Milan's surviving canals, the Naviglio Grande and Naviglio Pavese, meet at the Darsena basin. At sunset the towpaths fill with crowds hopping between aperitivo bars.`,tip:`An aperitivo drink usually comes with snacks. The last Sunday of most months brings a huge antiques market along the Naviglio Grande.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Navigli`},{id:`sant-ambrogio`,name:`Basilica of Sant'Ambrogio`,localName:`Basilica di Sant'Ambrogio`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`church`,`romanesque`,`history`,`free`],area:`Sant'Ambrogio`,lat:45.46243,lng:9.17581,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Founded by Milan's patron saint in the 4th century, this brick Romanesque basilica has a calm arcaded atrium, a golden altar and Saint Ambrose's remains in the crypt.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Basilica of Sant'Ambrogio`},{id:`biblioteca-ambrosiana`,name:`Pinacoteca & Biblioteca Ambrosiana`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`leonardo`,`caravaggio`,`library`,`rainy-day`],area:`Duomo`,lat:45.4631,lng:9.1854,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:4,description:`A 17th-century library and gallery with Caravaggio's Basket of Fruit, Raphael's cartoon for the School of Athens and pages from Leonardo's Codex Atlanticus.`,tip:`Displays of the Codex Atlanticus rotate, so each visit shows different pages.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Biblioteca Ambrosiana`},{id:`museo-del-novecento`,name:`Museo del Novecento`,category:`museum`,tags:[`modern-art`,`futurism`,`viewpoint`,`rainy-day`],area:`Duomo`,lat:45.46361,lng:9.19028,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:11,rating:4,description:`20th-century Italian art from Futurism to Arte Povera, climbing a spiral ramp to a glass-walled room that frames the Duomo's facade.`,tip:`Closed Mondays. The top-floor window onto Piazza del Duomo is worth the ticket alone.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Museo del Novecento`},{id:`royal-palace`,name:`Royal Palace of Milan`,localName:`Palazzo Reale`,category:`museum`,tags:[`exhibitions`,`palace`,`art`,`rainy-day`],area:`Duomo`,lat:45.4632,lng:9.1911,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:18,rating:3,description:`The former royal palace beside the Duomo is now Milan's main venue for blockbuster art exhibitions, from old masters to modern icons.`,tip:`Several days a week it stays open late into the evening; check what is showing before you go.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Royal Palace of Milan`},{id:`quadrilatero-della-moda`,name:`Fashion Quarter`,localName:`Quadrilatero della Moda`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`fashion`,`luxury`,`window-shopping`,`free`],area:`Montenapoleone`,lat:45.4699,lng:9.19534,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The square of streets around Via Montenapoleone and Via della Spiga is the heart of Italian high fashion, packed with flagship stores in elegant palazzi.`,tip:`Even if you are not buying, the window displays and people-watching are part of the Milan experience.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Quadrilatero della moda`},{id:`porta-nuova-bosco-verticale`,name:`Porta Nuova & Bosco Verticale`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`architecture`,`skyscrapers`,`modern`,`free`],area:`Porta Nuova / Isola`,lat:45.48583,lng:9.19028,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Milan's new skyline: the tree-covered towers of the Bosco Verticale, the fountains of Piazza Gae Aulenti and the Biblioteca degli Alberi park.`,tip:`Continue into the neighbouring Isola district for relaxed bars and trattorias.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Bosco Verticale`},{id:`fondazione-prada`,name:`Fondazione Prada`,category:`museum`,tags:[`contemporary-art`,`architecture`,`design`,`rainy-day`],area:`Porta Romana / Largo Isarco`,lat:45.444,lng:9.20541,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:22,rating:4,description:`Contemporary art in a former distillery remade by Rem Koolhaas's OMA, including a gold-leaf-clad tower and a white tower with sweeping views.`,tip:`Closed Tuesdays. Stop at Bar Luce, the retro cafe designed by Wes Anderson, at the entrance.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Fondazione Prada`},{id:`cimitero-monumentale`,name:`Monumental Cemetery`,localName:`Cimitero Monumentale`,category:`culture`,tags:[`cemetery`,`sculpture`,`architecture`,`free`,`quiet`],area:`Porta Garibaldi`,lat:45.48583,lng:9.17906,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`An open-air museum of funerary art, where Milan's wealthy families competed with ever more extravagant tombs, from Art Nouveau angels to modernist temples.`,tip:`Closed Mondays. Pick up a free map at the entrance to find the most remarkable tombs.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Cimitero Monumentale di Milano`},{id:`science-museum`,name:`Leonardo da Vinci Museum of Science and Technology`,localName:`Museo Nazionale Scienza e Tecnologia Leonardo da Vinci`,category:`family`,tags:[`science`,`leonardo`,`kids`,`submarine`,`rainy-day`],area:`Sant'Ambrogio`,lat:45.46302,lng:9.17124,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:4,description:`Italy's largest science museum, in a former monastery, with models built from Leonardo's drawings, steam trains, ships and a real submarine.`,tip:`The Enrico Toti submarine tour is booked separately on arrival; slots go fast at weekends. Closed Mondays.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Museo Nazionale Scienza e Tecnologia Leonardo da Vinci`},{id:`hangar-bicocca`,name:`Pirelli HangarBicocca`,category:`museum`,tags:[`contemporary-art`,`installation`,`free`,`industrial`,`rainy-day`],area:`Bicocca`,lat:45.52215,lng:9.22015,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A colossal former locomotive factory turned free contemporary art space, home to Anselm Kiefer's permanent Seven Heavenly Palaces towers.`,tip:`Open Thursday to Sunday only; take metro line 5 to Ponale.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`HangarBicocca`},{id:`poldi-pezzoli`,name:`Museo Poldi Pezzoli`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`house-museum`,`renaissance`,`rainy-day`],area:`Montenapoleone`,lat:45.46866,lng:9.19158,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:16,rating:3,description:`A 19th-century collector's mansion filled with Renaissance paintings, armour and clocks, best known for Pollaiolo's Portrait of a Young Woman.`,tip:`Closed Tuesdays.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Museo Poldi Pezzoli`},{id:`san-maurizio`,name:`San Maurizio al Monastero Maggiore`,category:`culture`,tags:[`church`,`frescoes`,`hidden-gem`,`free`],area:`Magenta`,lat:45.4655,lng:9.17892,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A plain facade on Corso Magenta hides walls covered floor to ceiling in 16th-century frescoes, earning it the nickname of Milan's Sistine Chapel.`,tip:`Walk through to the rear nuns' hall behind the altar, which is just as richly painted. Closed Mondays.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`San Maurizio al Monastero Maggiore`},{id:`colonne-di-san-lorenzo`,name:`Columns of San Lorenzo`,localName:`Colonne di San Lorenzo`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`roman`,`history`,`free`,`nightlife`],area:`Ticinese`,lat:45.4582,lng:9.181,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Sixteen Roman columns stand in front of the early-Christian Basilica of San Lorenzo. On warm evenings the piazza fills with young Milanese drinking under them.`,tip:`Peek into the basilica to see the 4th-century mosaics of the Chapel of Sant'Aquilino.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Colonne di San Lorenzo`},{id:`san-siro`,name:`San Siro Stadium Tour`,localName:`Stadio Giuseppe Meazza`,category:`family`,tags:[`football`,`stadium`,`sport`,`museum`],area:`San Siro`,lat:45.47806,lng:9.12389,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:35,rating:3,description:`The home of AC Milan and Inter, one of Europe's great football grounds. The tour visits the stands, dressing rooms and a museum of trophies and shirts.`,tip:`Tours are cut short or cancelled on match days. Better still, catch a game: tickets are sold on the clubs' official sites.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`San Siro`},{id:`villa-necchi-campiglio`,name:`Villa Necchi Campiglio`,category:`museum`,tags:[`house-museum`,`art-deco`,`garden`,`design`,`rainy-day`],area:`Porta Venezia`,lat:45.4683,lng:9.2018,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:4,description:`A sleek 1930s villa with a garden and swimming pool, preserved with its original furnishings and art collection; the setting of the film I Am Love.`,tip:`Visits are guided and run Wednesday to Sunday; the garden cafe is a peaceful place for coffee.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Villa Necchi Campiglio`},{id:`giardini-pubblici`,name:`Indro Montanelli Public Gardens`,localName:`Giardini Pubblici Indro Montanelli`,category:`nature`,tags:[`park`,`free`,`family`,`natural-history`],area:`Porta Venezia`,lat:45.47444,lng:9.2,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Milan's oldest public park, with shady avenues, ponds and playgrounds, plus the Natural History Museum and a planetarium on its edges.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Giardini Pubblici Indro Montanelli`},{id:`chinatown-paolo-sarpi`,name:`Chinatown & Via Paolo Sarpi`,category:`food`,tags:[`street-food`,`dumplings`,`neighbourhood`,`shopping`],area:`Chinatown`,lat:45.48139,lng:9.17667,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:3,description:`Italy's oldest Chinese community lines pedestrianised Via Paolo Sarpi with dumpling counters, bakeries, bubble-tea shops and Milanese delis side by side.`,tip:`Graze rather than sit down: hand-made ravioli and steamed buns cost a few euros each.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Chinatown, Milan`},{id:`camparino-in-galleria`,name:`Camparino in Galleria`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`aperitivo`,`historic`,`campari`,`cocktails`],area:`Duomo`,lat:45.46492,lng:9.18988,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:14,rating:3,description:`The historic bar at the Duomo entrance to the Galleria, where the Campari family served its bitter aperitif; order a Campari soda at the Art Nouveau counter.`,tip:`Drinks at the standing bar cost much less than at the tables.`,indoor:!0},{id:`armani-silos`,name:`Armani/Silos`,category:`museum`,tags:[`fashion`,`design`,`exhibitions`,`rainy-day`],area:`Tortona`,lat:45.45151,lng:9.16469,durationHours:1.25,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:16,rating:3,description:`Giorgio Armani's own fashion museum, in a converted grain silo in the Tortona design district, showing decades of his clothes and changing exhibitions.`,tip:`Opening days and exhibitions change; check the official site before going.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Armani/Silos`},{id:`triennale`,name:`Triennale Milano`,localName:`Triennale di Milano`,category:`museum`,tags:[`design`,`architecture`,`exhibitions`,`rainy-day`],area:`Castello`,lat:45.4724,lng:9.174,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:17,rating:3,description:`Milan's design museum, on the edge of Parco Sempione, with a permanent collection of Italian design and changing shows on architecture and art.`,tip:`Closed Mondays. The terrace restaurant has fine views over the park.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Triennale di Milano`},{id:`lake-como`,name:`Lake Como: Bellagio & Varenna Day Trip`,localName:`Lago di Como`,category:`nature`,tags:[`day-trip`,`lake`,`boat`,`villages`,`scenic`],area:`Lake Como`,lat:45.98333,lng:9.25,durationHours:9,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:40,rating:5,description:`Mountains plunge into a deep blue lake ringed by pastel villages and grand villas. Hop between Varenna, Bellagio and Menaggio on the passenger ferries.`,tip:`Take the train from Milano Centrale to Varenna (about 1 hour), then use the mid-lake ferries; a day pass is cheaper than single tickets.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Lake Como`},{id:`como-brunate-funicular`,name:`Como Town & Brunate Funicular`,localName:`Funicolare Como-Brunate`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`day-trip`,`funicular`,`viewpoint`,`lake`,`hiking`],area:`Lake Como`,lat:45.81838,lng:9.08942,durationHours:5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:4,description:`Stroll Como's lakefront and cathedral, then ride the steep funicular to the hill village of Brunate for sweeping views over the lake and the Alps.`,tip:`From Brunate, a 20-minute uphill walk to the Volta lighthouse gives an even wider panorama.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Como–Brunate funicular`},{id:`villa-del-balbianello`,name:`Villa del Balbianello`,category:`culture`,tags:[`day-trip`,`villa`,`gardens`,`lake`,`film-location`],area:`Lake Como`,lat:45.96509,lng:9.2025,durationHours:7,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:4,description:`A villa and terraced gardens perched on a wooded promontory of Lake Como, made famous by Star Wars and Casino Royale.`,tip:`Usually open mid-March to mid-November and closed on some weekdays; book online and arrive by water taxi from Lenno.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Villa del Balbianello`},{id:`bergamo-citta-alta`,name:`Bergamo Upper Town`,localName:`Bergamo Città Alta`,category:`culture`,tags:[`day-trip`,`medieval`,`walls`,`unesco`,`funicular`],area:`Bergamo`,lat:45.70404,lng:9.6629,durationHours:7,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:15,rating:4,description:`A hilltop medieval town ringed by Venetian walls, with the lovely Piazza Vecchia, the ornate Colleoni Chapel and a funicular from the lower town.`,tip:`Trains from Milano Centrale or Porta Garibaldi take about an hour; try polenta and casoncelli pasta for lunch.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Bergamo`},{id:`borromean-islands`,name:`Borromean Islands, Lake Maggiore`,localName:`Isole Borromee`,category:`nature`,tags:[`day-trip`,`lake`,`gardens`,`palace`,`boat`],area:`Lake Maggiore`,lat:45.89547,lng:8.52723,durationHours:9,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:60,rating:4,description:`From Stresa, boats run to Isola Bella's baroque palace and terraced gardens with white peacocks, Isola Madre's botanical gardens and the fishing village of Isola dei Pescatori.`,tip:`The palaces and gardens open from late March to early November. Buy a combined boat pass in Stresa.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Borromean Islands`}],foods:[{name:`Risotto alla Milanese`,description:`Saffron-gold risotto made with beef marrow and butter, often served alongside ossobuco.`},{name:`Milanese Veal Cutlet`,localName:`Cotoletta alla Milanese`,description:`A bone-in veal chop, breaded and fried in butter until golden; the thin, plate-sized version is called orecchia d'elefante.`},{name:`Ossobuco`,description:`Cross-cut veal shank braised slowly in white wine and broth, topped with lemon-and-parsley gremolata; scoop out the marrow.`},{name:`Panzerotti`,description:`Fried half-moon turnovers stuffed with tomato and mozzarella, the classic Milan street snack near the Duomo.`},{name:`Panettone`,description:`Milan's tall, airy sweet bread with candied orange and raisins, a Christmas staple sold by top pastry shops all year.`},{name:`Cassoeula`,description:`A rich winter stew of pork ribs, sausage and trotters slow-cooked with Savoy cabbage, often served with polenta.`}]},{id:`naples`,name:`Naples`,localName:`Napoli`,lat:40.85183,lng:14.26812,timezone:`Europe/Rome`,tagline:`Pizza, Baroque chapels and Vesuvius over the bay`,description:`Loud, layered and gloriously alive, Naples packs Greek streets, Baroque churches and one of the world's great archaeology museums into a historic centre that is still lived in. Eat the pizza where it was born, then head out to Pompeii, Vesuvius, Capri or the Amalfi Coast.`,idealDays:[3,5],places:[{id:`national-archaeological-museum`,name:`National Archaeological Museum`,localName:`Museo Archeologico Nazionale (MANN)`,category:`museum`,tags:[`iconic`,`archaeology`,`pompeii`,`mosaics`,`rainy-day`],area:`Centro Storico`,lat:40.85353,lng:14.25057,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:25,rating:5,description:`The treasure house of Pompeii and Herculaneum: the Alexander Mosaic, frescoes lifted from Roman villas, the colossal Farnese sculptures and the notorious Secret Cabinet.`,tip:`Closed Tuesdays. See it before you visit Pompeii, so the ruins make more sense.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`National Archaeological Museum, Naples`},{id:`sansevero-chapel`,name:`Sansevero Chapel & the Veiled Christ`,localName:`Museo Cappella Sansevero`,category:`museum`,tags:[`iconic`,`sculpture`,`baroque`,`rainy-day`],area:`Centro Storico`,lat:40.84942,lng:14.25478,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:14,rating:5,description:`A small Baroque chapel holding Giuseppe Sanmartino's Veiled Christ, a marble body under a shroud so fine it looks like real cloth, plus two eerie anatomical machines in the crypt.`,tip:`Book a timed ticket online; queues build by mid-morning. Photography is not allowed inside.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Cappella Sansevero`},{id:`spaccanapoli`,name:`Spaccanapoli`,category:`culture`,tags:[`iconic`,`street`,`walk`,`free`,`historic-centre`],area:`Centro Storico`,lat:40.84847,lng:14.25404,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`The long, dead-straight street that 'splits Naples' through the old Greek grid, lined with churches, pastry shops, shrines and scooters weaving through the crowds.`,tip:`Walk it end to end from Piazza del Gesù Nuovo, then loop back along parallel Via dei Tribunali.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Spaccanapoli (street)`},{id:`napoli-sotterranea`,name:`Naples Underground`,localName:`Napoli Sotterranea`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`underground`,`tour`,`history`,`rainy-day`,`kids`],area:`Centro Storico`,lat:40.85108,lng:14.25685,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:17,rating:4,description:`A guided descent 40 metres below Via dei Tribunali into Greek quarries, Roman cisterns and Second World War air-raid shelters, plus the remains of a Roman theatre hidden inside a basso home.`,tip:`Tours leave on the hour in English; one passage is a narrow candle-lit squeeze, skippable if you are claustrophobic.`,indoor:!0},{id:`via-san-gregorio-armeno`,name:`Via San Gregorio Armeno`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`nativity`,`crafts`,`street`,`free`,`christmas`],area:`Centro Storico`,lat:40.85044,lng:14.25748,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`The narrow "Christmas alley" of workshops making presepi, hand-crafted nativity scenes crammed with shepherds, pizzaioli, saints and caricatures of footballers and politicians.`,tip:`Open all year, but packed from November to early January.`,wiki:`Via San Gregorio Armeno`,indoor:!1},{id:`naples-cathedral`,name:`Naples Cathedral`,localName:`Duomo di Napoli`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`church`,`san-gennaro`,`free`,`rainy-day`],area:`Centro Storico`,lat:40.85267,lng:14.25967,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Gothic cathedral with a dazzling Baroque chapel of San Gennaro, the city's patron saint, whose dried blood is said to liquefy three times a year.`,tip:`Free to enter; the Treasure of San Gennaro museum next door charges a separate fee.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Naples Cathedral`},{id:`san-lorenzo-maggiore`,name:`San Lorenzo Maggiore & Excavations`,category:`museum`,tags:[`church`,`archaeology`,`underground`,`rainy-day`],area:`Centro Storico`,lat:40.85075,lng:14.25796,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:11,rating:4,description:`A soaring Gothic church above an excavated Roman market street, with shops, a bakery and a treasury still standing where ancient Neapolis' forum once traded.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`San Lorenzo Maggiore, Naples`},{id:`pio-monte-della-misericordia`,name:`Pio Monte della Misericordia`,category:`museum`,tags:[`caravaggio`,`art`,`baroque`,`rainy-day`],area:`Centro Storico`,lat:40.85222,lng:14.26036,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:11,rating:4,description:`A charitable institution's octagonal chapel where Caravaggio's The Seven Works of Mercy still hangs above the altar it was painted for, with a picture gallery upstairs.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Pio Monte della Misericordia`},{id:`gesu-nuovo`,name:`Church of Gesù Nuovo`,localName:`Chiesa del Gesù Nuovo`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`church`,`baroque`,`free`,`rainy-day`],area:`Centro Storico`,lat:40.84822,lng:14.25036,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Behind a severe diamond-point stone facade lies an explosion of coloured marble, frescoes and gilt, one of the richest Baroque interiors in the city.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Gesù Nuovo`},{id:`santa-chiara-cloister`,name:`Santa Chiara Monastery & Majolica Cloister`,localName:`Monastero di Santa Chiara`,category:`culture`,tags:[`cloister`,`majolica`,`garden`,`peaceful`],area:`Centro Storico`,lat:40.84694,lng:14.25268,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:8,rating:4,description:`A calm garden cloister lined with hand-painted majolica tiles of vines, lemons and country scenes, beside the vast Gothic basilica of Naples' royal Angevin rulers.`,tip:`The basilica is free; the ticket covers the cloister, museum and Roman bath ruins.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Santa Chiara, Naples`},{id:`catacombs-of-san-gennaro`,name:`Catacombs of San Gennaro`,localName:`Catacombe di San Gennaro`,category:`culture`,tags:[`catacombs`,`underground`,`early-christian`,`rainy-day`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Rione Sanità`,lat:40.86378,lng:14.24706,durationHours:1.25,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:13,rating:4,description:`Two levels of early-Christian burial halls carved into the tuff hillside, with some of southern Italy's oldest frescoes, run by a youth cooperative from the Sanità district.`,tip:`Visits are guided; the ticket also covers the Catacombs of San Gaudioso in the Sanità below.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Catacombs of San Gennaro`},{id:`fontanelle-cemetery`,name:`Fontanelle Cemetery`,localName:`Cimitero delle Fontanelle`,category:`culture`,tags:[`ossuary`,`cave`,`folklore`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Rione Sanità`,lat:40.85803,lng:14.23901,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:9,rating:4,description:`A cavernous tuff quarry stacked with thousands of anonymous skulls, once 'adopted' and tended by Neapolitans hoping for favours from the souls of the dead.`,tip:`Reopened in April 2026 after five years of works; booking online is required and it is closed Wednesdays.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Fontanelle cemetery`},{id:`capodimonte`,name:`Capodimonte Museum & Royal Park`,localName:`Museo e Real Bosco di Capodimonte`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`caravaggio`,`palace`,`park`,`rainy-day`],area:`Capodimonte`,lat:40.86717,lng:14.25036,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:17,rating:4,description:`A Bourbon hunting palace on the hill holding one of Italy's great picture galleries, from Titian and Raphael to Caravaggio's Flagellation, set in a huge free park.`,tip:`Closed Wednesdays. Rarely crowded; combine with the Catacombs of San Gennaro just downhill.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Museo di Capodimonte`},{id:`piazza-del-plebiscito`,name:`Piazza del Plebiscito`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`square`,`free`,`night-view`],area:`San Ferdinando`,lat:40.83586,lng:14.24853,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Naples' grandest square, a vast open space framed by the Royal Palace and the colonnaded church of San Francesco di Paola, glowing gold after dark.`,tip:`Try walking blindfolded between the two equestrian statues; locals say almost nobody makes it.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Piazza del Plebiscito`},{id:`royal-palace`,name:`Royal Palace of Naples`,localName:`Palazzo Reale`,category:`museum`,tags:[`palace`,`bourbon`,`history`,`rainy-day`],area:`San Ferdinando`,lat:40.83611,lng:14.25001,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:17,rating:4,description:`The Bourbon kings' palace, with a monumental marble staircase, gilded royal apartments, a private court theatre and a roof garden over the port.`,tip:`Closed Wednesdays.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Royal Palace of Naples`},{id:`teatro-di-san-carlo`,name:`Teatro di San Carlo`,category:`culture`,tags:[`opera`,`ballet`,`theatre`,`night-out`],area:`San Ferdinando`,lat:40.83747,lng:14.24961,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:70,rating:4,description:`Europe's oldest continuously active opera house, opened in 1737: a red-and-gold horseshoe of six tiers of boxes facing the royal box. An opera or ballet here is a proper night out.`,tip:`Upper-tier seats can be cheap; daytime guided tours run if you cannot catch a performance.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Teatro di San Carlo`},{id:`galleria-umberto`,name:`Galleria Umberto I`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`architecture`,`arcade`,`free`,`rainy-day`],area:`San Ferdinando`,lat:40.83833,lng:14.24955,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A soaring 1890s shopping arcade under a glass-and-iron dome, with a zodiac mosaic floor, opposite the San Carlo opera house.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Galleria Umberto I`},{id:`castel-nuovo`,name:`Castel Nuovo`,localName:`Maschio Angioino`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`castle`,`medieval`,`museum`,`port`],area:`San Ferdinando`,lat:40.83844,lng:14.25275,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:7,rating:3,description:`Five round towers and a white marble Renaissance triumphal arch guard this harbourside castle, now home to the civic museum and the frescoed Palatine Chapel.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Castel Nuovo`},{id:`galleria-borbonica`,name:`Bourbon Tunnel`,localName:`Galleria Borbonica`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`underground`,`tour`,`wwii`,`rainy-day`,`kids`],area:`Chiaia`,lat:40.83548,lng:14.24628,durationHours:1.25,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:17,rating:4,description:`A royal escape tunnel dug for the Bourbon king, later an air-raid shelter and a police car pound, now a guided walk past vintage cars and scooters rusting in the dark.`,tip:`Visits are by guided tour only; the standard route is easy walking.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Bourbon Tunnel`},{id:`lungomare-castel-dell-ovo`,name:`Seafront & Castel dell'Ovo`,localName:`Lungomare e Castel dell'Ovo`,category:`nature`,tags:[`seafront`,`walk`,`free`,`sunset`,`night-view`,`iconic`],area:`Santa Lucia`,lat:40.82803,lng:14.24748,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`Stroll the traffic-free promenade along the bay with Vesuvius on the horizon to the Norman sea castle on its islet and the little fishing harbour of Borgo Marinari.`,tip:`The castle interior has been closed for long restoration works; the seafront and harbour are best at sunset.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Castel dell'Ovo`},{id:`chiaia-baretti`,name:`Chiaia Bar Alleys`,localName:`Baretti di Chiaia`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`bars`,`aperitivo`,`locals`,`night-out`],area:`Chiaia`,lat:40.83513,lng:14.23943,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:20,rating:3,description:`Young Naples spills out of the tiny bars around Vico Belledonne and Via Bisignano late into the night, drinks in hand on the cobbles of the city's smartest district.`,tip:`Things only get going after 10pm, busiest from Thursday to Saturday.`,indoor:!1},{id:`quartieri-spagnoli`,name:`Spanish Quarter & Maradona Mural`,localName:`Quartieri Spagnoli`,category:`culture`,tags:[`street-art`,`football`,`neighbourhood`,`free`,`local-life`],area:`Quartieri Spagnoli`,lat:40.84138,lng:14.24511,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A dense grid of steep alleys strung with washing lines, street shrines and scooters, centred on Largo Maradona, a shrine-like square to the football god of Naples.`,tip:`Wander in from Via Toledo; keep valuables out of sight as in any crowded area.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Quartieri Spagnoli`},{id:`toledo-metro-station`,name:`Toledo Metro Station`,localName:`Stazione Toledo`,category:`culture`,tags:[`art`,`architecture`,`metro`,`rainy-day`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Via Toledo`,lat:40.84284,lng:14.24873,durationHours:.25,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:2,rating:3,description:`One of Europe's most striking metro stations: escalators sink into a deep-blue mosaic 'sea crater' lit by a shaft of light, part of the city's Art Stations.`,tip:`You need a metro ticket to reach the platforms; the Sea of Light shaft is between the escalators.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Toledo station (Naples)`},{id:`castel-sant-elmo`,name:`Castel Sant'Elmo`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`castle`,`viewpoint`,`panorama`],area:`Vomero`,lat:40.84368,lng:14.23906,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:6,rating:4,description:`A star-shaped hilltop fortress whose ramparts give the best panorama of Naples: the old town's domes, the bay and Vesuvius all at once.`,tip:`Take the Montesanto or Centrale funicular up to Vomero to save the climb.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Castel Sant'Elmo`},{id:`certosa-di-san-martino`,name:`Certosa di San Martino`,category:`museum`,tags:[`monastery`,`nativity`,`baroque`,`viewpoint`,`rainy-day`],area:`Vomero`,lat:40.84308,lng:14.24056,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:7,rating:4,description:`A former Carthusian monastery below Sant'Elmo with a lavish Baroque church, a vast nativity-scene collection and terraced gardens looking over the bay.`,tip:`Closed Wednesdays. Do it on the same trip as Castel Sant'Elmo next door.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Certosa di San Martino`},{id:`villa-floridiana`,name:`Villa Floridiana`,category:`nature`,tags:[`park`,`garden`,`free`,`viewpoint`,`kids`],area:`Vomero`,lat:40.84118,lng:14.22998,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Shady 19th-century gardens on the Vomero hill with a belvedere over the bay and a neoclassical villa housing a ceramics museum.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Villa Floridiana`},{id:`pignasecca-market`,name:`Pignasecca Market`,localName:`Mercato della Pignasecca`,category:`food`,tags:[`market`,`street-food`,`local-life`,`free`],area:`Montesanto`,lat:40.84542,lng:14.24655,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The city's oldest street market, a noisy jumble of fishmongers, fruit stalls, bakeries and friggitorie frying snacks for shoppers.`,tip:`Liveliest in the morning; graze on a cuoppo of fried things as you go.`,indoor:!1},{id:`parco-virgiliano`,name:`Parco Virgiliano`,category:`nature`,tags:[`viewpoint`,`sunset`,`park`,`free`,`night-view`],area:`Posillipo`,lat:40.79848,lng:14.17909,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A clifftop park at the tip of Posillipo with sweeping views over the islands of Nisida, Procida and Capri; a favourite local spot to watch the sun go down.`,tip:`Take a bus or taxi up; it is a long climb from the Mergellina seafront.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Parco Virgiliano`},{id:`gaiola-underwater-park`,name:`Gaiola Underwater Park`,localName:`Parco Sommerso di Gaiola`,category:`nature`,tags:[`sea`,`swimming`,`snorkelling`,`ruins`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Posillipo`,lat:40.79193,lng:14.18696,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A marine protected area at the foot of Posillipo where clear water laps Roman villa ruins and two tiny islets joined by a footbridge.`,tip:`Beach access is free but capped and booked online in summer; snorkel and glass-bottom boat tours run from the visitor centre.`,indoor:!1},{id:`herculaneum`,name:`Herculaneum`,localName:`Scavi di Ercolano`,category:`culture`,tags:[`archaeology`,`roman`,`unesco`,`iconic`],area:`Ercolano`,lat:40.80588,lng:14.34772,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:16,rating:5,description:`Smaller and better preserved than Pompeii, this Roman town buried by Vesuvius still has wooden beams, two-storey houses and vivid frescoes, all easily covered in a morning.`,tip:`Twenty minutes from Naples on the Circumvesuviana to Ercolano Scavi. Closed Wednesdays.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Herculaneum`},{id:`mount-vesuvius`,name:`Mount Vesuvius`,localName:`Vesuvio`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`volcano`,`hike`,`viewpoint`,`iconic`],area:`Vesuvius National Park`,lat:40.82139,lng:14.42611,durationHours:4,bestTime:[`morning`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:4,description:`Hike the last 30 minutes up the volcano that buried Pompeii to peer into the steaming crater, with the whole Bay of Naples spread out below.`,tip:`Crater tickets are timed and sold online only; shuttle buses run from Ercolano and Pompeii. The path closes in high wind.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Mount Vesuvius`},{id:`pompeii`,name:`Pompeii`,localName:`Scavi di Pompei`,category:`culture`,tags:[`iconic`,`archaeology`,`roman`,`unesco`,`day-trip`],area:`Pompei`,lat:40.74896,lng:14.48463,durationHours:6,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:5,description:`The Roman city frozen by Vesuvius in AD 79: whole streets of shops, bakeries, villas, an amphitheatre and haunting plaster casts of its victims.`,tip:`Book a named ticket online, start early and bring water and a hat; there is little shade. Circumvesuviana train to Pompei Scavi.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Pompeii`},{id:`capri`,name:`Capri`,category:`nature`,tags:[`island`,`boat`,`day-trip`,`viewpoint`,`iconic`],area:`Capri`,lat:40.55076,lng:14.24258,durationHours:8,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:70,rating:4,description:`The glamorous island across the bay: ride the funicular to the Piazzetta, walk to the Gardens of Augustus over the Faraglioni rocks and take the chairlift up Monte Solaro in Anacapri.`,tip:`Hydrofoils from Molo Beverello take about 50 minutes. The Blue Grotto shuts in choppy seas.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Capri`},{id:`amalfi-coast`,name:`Amalfi Coast`,localName:`Costiera Amalfitana`,category:`nature`,tags:[`coast`,`scenic-drive`,`day-trip`,`unesco`,`iconic`],area:`Amalfi Coast`,lat:40.62809,lng:14.48467,durationHours:10,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:60,rating:5,description:`Pastel villages tumble down cliffs above the sea from Positano to Amalfi and Ravello, linked by a dizzying coast road and summer ferries.`,tip:`A long day: train to Sorrento, then SITA bus or ferry along the coast. Ferries are calmer than the bus in high season.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Amalfi Coast`}],foods:[{name:`Neapolitan Pizza`,localName:`Pizza Napoletana`,description:`Soft, puffy-rimmed pizza blistered in a wood-fired oven in about 90 seconds; the margherita and marinara are the classics.`},{name:`Pizza Fritta`,description:`Pizza dough folded around ricotta, provola, pork crackling and tomato, then deep-fried golden: the street pizza of old Naples.`},{name:`Neapolitan Ragù`,localName:`Ragù Napoletano`,description:`A Sunday sauce of whole cuts of beef and pork simmered for hours in tomato until dark and rich, served with ziti or rigatoni.`},{name:`Sfogliatella`,description:`Shell-shaped pastry of crackling, paper-thin layers (riccia) or soft shortcrust (frolla) filled with orange-scented ricotta and semolina.`},{name:`Babà`,description:`A small, mushroom-shaped yeast cake soaked in rum syrup, sold in every pastry shop in town.`},{name:`Pastiera`,description:`Easter tart of ricotta, cooked wheat berries and candied citrus scented with orange-flower water, now made all year round.`}]},{id:`bologna`,name:`Bologna`,lat:44.4949,lng:11.3426,timezone:`Europe/Rome`,tagline:`Red rooftops, endless porticoes and the home of ragù`,description:`Italy's great food city wears its nicknames well: la dotta for Europe's oldest university, la rossa for its terracotta rooftops and la grassa for tagliatelle, tortellini and mortadella. Forty kilometres of porticoes shelter medieval squares, leaning towers and lively student bars, and Modena, Parma and the mosaics of Ravenna are short train rides away.`,idealDays:[2,4],places:[{id:`piazza-maggiore`,name:`Piazza Maggiore`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`square`,`free`,`people-watching`,`night-view`],area:`Piazza Maggiore`,lat:44.49366,lng:11.34305,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`Bologna's grand main square, framed by the unfinished brick face of San Petronio, the city hall and the Renaissance Palazzo del Podestà.`,tip:`Under the Voltone del Podestà on the square's north side, whisper into a corner and a friend in the opposite corner will hear you clearly.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Piazza Maggiore`},{id:`basilica-di-san-petronio`,name:`Basilica of San Petronio`,localName:`Basilica di San Petronio`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`church`,`gothic`,`free`,`rainy-day`],area:`Piazza Maggiore`,lat:44.49274,lng:11.34303,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`One of the largest brick churches in the world, its half-clad façade hiding a soaring Gothic nave with a 67-metre meridian line set into the floor.`,tip:`Entry is free; a small fee lets you photograph inside. Bags are checked at the door, so travel light.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`San Petronio, Bologna`},{id:`due-torri-bologna`,name:`The Two Towers`,localName:`Le Due Torri`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`iconic`,`towers`,`medieval`,`free`,`photo-spot`],area:`Piazza di Porta Ravegnana`,lat:44.4942,lng:11.34677,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`The twin leaning towers of Asinelli and Garisenda, survivors of the dozens of family towers that once bristled over medieval Bologna.`,tip:`The Garisenda is fenced off for long-term stabilisation work and climbs of the Asinelli have been suspended, so admire them from the street and climb the Clock Tower for views instead.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Two Towers, Bologna`},{id:`fontana-del-nettuno`,name:`Fountain of Neptune`,localName:`Fontana del Nettuno`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`fountain`,`renaissance`,`sculpture`,`free`,`photo-spot`],area:`Piazza Maggiore`,lat:44.49427,lng:11.34266,durationHours:.25,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Giambologna's muscular bronze Neptune of the 1560s, standing over water-spouting sirens in the square beside Piazza Maggiore.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Fountain of Neptune, Bologna`},{id:`archiginnasio-anatomical-theatre`,name:`Archiginnasio and Anatomical Theatre`,localName:`Archiginnasio e Teatro Anatomico`,category:`museum`,tags:[`university`,`library`,`history`,`rainy-day`,`iconic`],area:`Piazza Maggiore`,lat:44.49198,lng:11.34352,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:4,rating:5,description:`The 16th-century seat of Bologna's university, its walls and vaults covered in thousands of student coats of arms, with a carved wooden theatre where anatomy lessons were held.`,tip:`The courtyard and loggias are free; a small ticket covers the Anatomical Theatre and the Stabat Mater reading room.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Archiginnasio of Bologna`},{id:`santo-stefano-seven-churches`,name:`Santo Stefano (Seven Churches)`,localName:`Basilica di Santo Stefano`,category:`culture`,tags:[`church`,`romanesque`,`free`,`iconic`,`rainy-day`],area:`Santo Stefano`,lat:44.49203,lng:11.34872,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`A labyrinth of interlinked Romanesque churches, cloisters and courtyards, known locally as the Sette Chiese, on a sloping cobbled piazza.`,tip:`Linger in the triangular Piazza Santo Stefano afterwards; it's one of the city's prettiest spots for an evening drink.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Santo Stefano, Bologna`},{id:`san-luca-portico-walk`,name:`Portico of San Luca and Sanctuary`,localName:`Portico e Santuario di San Luca`,category:`adventure`,tags:[`walk`,`viewpoint`,`free`,`iconic`,`unesco`],area:`Colle della Guardia`,lat:44.4791,lng:11.29817,durationHours:3,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:5,description:`The world's longest portico, 666 arches climbing nearly four kilometres from Porta Saragozza up to a hilltop sanctuary looking over the city and the hills.`,tip:`Start at Porta Saragozza; the steep part begins at the Meloncello arch. The little San Luca Express tourist train goes up if you only want the view.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Madonna di San Luca, Bologna`},{id:`quadrilatero-market-streets`,name:`Quadrilatero Market Streets`,localName:`Quadrilatero`,category:`food`,tags:[`market`,`deli`,`aperitivo`,`free`,`iconic`],area:`Quadrilatero`,lat:44.49332,lng:11.34422,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:4,description:`A medieval grid of narrow lanes just off Piazza Maggiore, crammed with delis, fishmongers and greengrocers, and spilling over with aperitivo tables at dusk.`,tip:`Via Pescherie Vecchie and Via Drapperie are the heart of it; order a tagliere of cured meats and cheese with a glass of Pignoletto.`,indoor:!1},{id:`finestrella-via-piella`,name:`Little Window on Via Piella`,localName:`Finestrella di Via Piella`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`hidden-gem`,`canal`,`free`,`photo-spot`],area:`University Quarter`,lat:44.49857,lng:11.34516,durationHours:.25,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A shutter in a wall that opens onto the Canale delle Moline, a surprise glimpse of Bologna's mostly hidden network of medieval canals.`,tip:`There's often a short queue for photos; look from the other side of the bridge on Via Oberdan too.`,indoor:!1},{id:`pinacoteca-nazionale-bologna`,name:`National Picture Gallery`,localName:`Pinacoteca Nazionale di Bologna`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`renaissance`,`baroque`,`rainy-day`],area:`University Quarter`,lat:44.49791,lng:11.35362,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:11,rating:4,description:`The city's main art gallery, strong on the Bolognese school, from Gothic altarpieces to the Carracci, Guido Reni and Raphael's Ecstasy of Saint Cecilia.`,tip:`Closed on Mondays; the first Sunday of the month is free.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Pinacoteca Nazionale di Bologna`},{id:`mambo-bologna`,name:`MAMbo – Museum of Modern Art and Museo Morandi`,localName:`MAMbo – Museo d'Arte Moderna di Bologna`,category:`museum`,tags:[`art`,`modern`,`morandi`,`rainy-day`],area:`Manifattura delle Arti`,lat:44.50255,lng:11.33696,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:7,rating:3,description:`Contemporary art in a former municipal bakery, which also houses the Museo Morandi's quiet still lifes of bottles and jars by Bologna's best-loved painter.`,tip:`Closed on Mondays; the Morandi rooms are the highlight for most visitors.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Museo d'Arte Moderna di Bologna`},{id:`museo-civico-archeologico-bologna`,name:`Civic Archaeological Museum`,localName:`Museo Civico Archeologico`,category:`museum`,tags:[`archaeology`,`etruscan`,`egypt`,`rainy-day`],area:`Piazza Maggiore`,lat:44.49271,lng:11.34386,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:7,rating:4,description:`One of Italy's finest Egyptian collections plus Etruscan and Roman finds from ancient Felsina, the city that became Bologna, in a palace beside San Petronio.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Archaeological Civic Museum of Bologna`},{id:`torre-dell-orologio-bologna`,name:`Clock Tower and Municipal Art Collections`,localName:`Torre dell'Orologio e Collezioni Comunali d'Arte`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`viewpoint`,`tower`,`art`,`palace`],area:`Piazza Maggiore`,lat:44.49365,lng:11.3422,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:4,description:`A climb up the city hall's clock tower to a terrace over Piazza Maggiore's rooftops and the Two Towers, combined with the palace's frescoed art collections.`,tip:`Buy timed tickets at the Bologna Welcome office on the square or online; closed shoes are required and under-8s are not allowed up.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Palazzo d'Accursio`},{id:`basilica-di-san-domenico`,name:`Basilica of San Domenico`,localName:`Basilica di San Domenico`,category:`culture`,tags:[`church`,`michelangelo`,`free`,`rainy-day`],area:`Santo Stefano`,lat:44.48947,lng:11.3446,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`Resting place of Saint Dominic, whose marble tomb includes small statues carved by a young Michelangelo.`,tip:`Coins light up the Arca di San Domenico; the chapel is to the right of the nave.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`San Domenico, Bologna`},{id:`santa-maria-della-vita`,name:`Santa Maria della Vita`,category:`culture`,tags:[`church`,`sculpture`,`hidden-gem`,`rainy-day`],area:`Quadrilatero`,lat:44.49344,lng:11.34461,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:6,rating:4,description:`A baroque church in the market streets hiding Niccolò dell'Arca's Lamentation, seven life-size terracotta figures frozen in raw, wailing grief.`,tip:`Your ticket also covers the oratory upstairs with another terracotta group.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Santa Maria della Vita`},{id:`museo-storia-bologna`,name:`Museum of the History of Bologna`,localName:`Museo della Storia di Bologna – Palazzo Pepoli`,category:`museum`,tags:[`history`,`kids`,`interactive`,`rainy-day`],area:`Santo Stefano`,lat:44.49235,lng:11.34655,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:11,rating:3,description:`Interactive galleries in a medieval palace telling 2,500 years of Bologna, from Etruscan Felsina to the porticoes, towers and university.`,tip:`A good first stop to make sense of the city; closed on Mondays.`,indoor:!0},{id:`mercato-delle-erbe`,name:`Mercato delle Erbe`,category:`food`,tags:[`market`,`food-hall`,`local`,`rainy-day`],area:`Marconi`,lat:44.49607,lng:11.33828,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:12,rating:4,description:`Bologna's covered food market, where locals shop for produce by day and the food counters and small eateries around the edges fill up in the evening.`,tip:`Market stalls close in the early afternoon (and on Sundays); the eateries stay open for dinner.`,indoor:!0},{id:`via-del-pratello`,name:`Via del Pratello`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`bars`,`students`,`osterie`,`free`,`local`],area:`Pratello`,lat:44.49553,lng:11.333,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:10,rating:4,description:`A long porticoed street of osterie, wine bars and pubs that becomes one of the liveliest, most local night-time strips in the city.`,tip:`Start with dinner at one of the trattorie, then bar-hop; it gets busiest after 10pm on weekends.`,indoor:!1},{id:`giardini-margherita`,name:`Giardini Margherita`,category:`nature`,tags:[`park`,`free`,`picnic`,`kids`,`local`],area:`Giardini Margherita`,lat:44.4835,lng:11.3525,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The city's largest park, with a lake, shady lawns, jogging paths and kiosks, just outside the old walls south of the centre.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Giardini Margherita`},{id:`biblioteca-salaborsa`,name:`Salaborsa Library`,localName:`Biblioteca Salaborsa`,category:`culture`,tags:[`library`,`roman-ruins`,`free`,`rainy-day`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Piazza Maggiore`,lat:44.49477,lng:11.34142,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A public library in a glass-roofed Liberty-style hall, where a glass floor reveals Roman and medieval ruins excavated beneath your feet.`,tip:`Free to enter; the excavations below can be visited on certain days for free too.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Biblioteca Salaborsa`},{id:`basilica-di-san-francesco-bologna`,name:`Basilica of San Francesco`,localName:`Basilica di San Francesco`,category:`culture`,tags:[`church`,`gothic`,`free`,`tombs`],area:`Marconi`,lat:44.49476,lng:11.33565,durationHours:.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`An early French-style Gothic church with flying buttresses, a marble altarpiece and the raised tombs of medieval law professors outside.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`San Francesco, Bologna`},{id:`museo-della-musica-bologna`,name:`International Museum and Library of Music`,localName:`Museo internazionale e biblioteca della musica`,category:`museum`,tags:[`music`,`mozart`,`palace`,`rainy-day`],area:`Strada Maggiore`,lat:44.49287,lng:11.35025,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:7,rating:3,description:`Rare scores, instruments and portraits from Padre Martini's collection, including a young Mozart's Bologna exam, in a frescoed palazzo on Strada Maggiore.`,tip:`Closed on Mondays.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Museo internazionale e biblioteca della musica`},{id:`palazzo-poggi-museum`,name:`Palazzo Poggi Museum`,localName:`Museo di Palazzo Poggi`,category:`museum`,tags:[`science`,`anatomy`,`university`,`rainy-day`,`hidden-gem`],area:`University Quarter`,lat:44.49661,lng:11.3526,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:6,rating:4,description:`The university's 18th-century science collections, from wax anatomical models and obstetric figures to maps, ships and natural history, under frescoed ceilings.`,tip:`Closed on Mondays; the wax anatomy rooms are not for the squeamish.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Palazzo Poggi`},{id:`osteria-del-sole`,name:`Osteria del Sole`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`wine-bar`,`historic`,`local`,`hidden-gem`],area:`Quadrilatero`,lat:44.49379,lng:11.34435,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:6,rating:4,description:`A bare-bones wine tavern in business since the 15th century, where you buy the wine and bring your own food from the market stalls outside.`,tip:`Cash only, no food served and it closes by early evening, so come for an afternoon glass with a bag of deli treats.`,indoor:!0},{id:`cantina-bentivoglio`,name:`Cantina Bentivoglio`,category:`nightlife`,tags:[`jazz`,`live-music`,`wine-bar`],area:`University Quarter`,lat:44.49817,lng:11.34912,durationHours:2.5,bestTime:[`evening`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:35,rating:4,description:`A long-running jazz club in the brick-vaulted cellars of a Renaissance palace, with live sets most nights over dinner and wine.`,tip:`Book a table for dinner if you want to sit near the stage; music usually starts around 10pm.`,indoor:!0},{id:`ducati-museum`,name:`Ducati Museum`,localName:`Museo Ducati`,category:`museum`,tags:[`motorbikes`,`design`,`racing`,`rainy-day`],area:`Borgo Panigale`,lat:44.51616,lng:11.26843,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:22,rating:3,description:`The motorcycle maker's museum at its Borgo Panigale works, tracing Ducati's history and racing wins, with factory tours bookable separately.`,tip:`Book the factory tour well ahead; it runs on weekdays only. Bus 13 runs from the centre.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Ducati Museum`},{id:`villa-ghigi-park`,name:`Villa Ghigi Park`,localName:`Parco Villa Ghigi`,category:`nature`,tags:[`park`,`hills`,`viewpoint`,`free`,`walk`],area:`Colli Bolognesi`,lat:44.47625,lng:11.32892,durationHours:2,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`Hillside meadows, orchards and woods just above the city walls, with paths opening onto views of the red rooftops below.`,tip:`Combine with a walk up Via San Mamolo; it is a short bus ride from the centre.`,indoor:!1},{id:`strada-maggiore-servi`,name:`Strada Maggiore and Santa Maria dei Servi`,category:`landmark`,tags:[`porticoes`,`church`,`free`,`walk`,`unesco`],area:`Strada Maggiore`,lat:44.49161,lng:11.35263,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:4,description:`A stroll along the old Via Emilia under some of the city's oldest and grandest porticoes, ending at the elegant arcaded church of Santa Maria dei Servi.`,tip:`Look up near Casa Isolani for the wooden medieval portico with arrows said to be stuck in its beams.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Santa Maria dei Servi, Bologna`},{id:`san-giacomo-maggiore-bologna`,name:`San Giacomo Maggiore and Oratory of Santa Cecilia`,localName:`San Giacomo Maggiore e Oratorio di Santa Cecilia`,category:`culture`,tags:[`church`,`frescoes`,`free`,`hidden-gem`,`rainy-day`],area:`University Quarter`,lat:44.4966,lng:11.3499,durationHours:.75,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`The Bentivoglio family's church, with a richly painted chapel, and next door a small oratory frescoed with the life of Saint Cecilia.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`San Giacomo Maggiore, Bologna`},{id:`museo-patrimonio-industriale`,name:`Museum of Industrial Heritage`,localName:`Museo del Patrimonio Industriale`,category:`family`,tags:[`kids`,`industry`,`silk`,`rainy-day`],area:`Bolognina`,lat:44.52171,lng:11.33459,durationHours:1.5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:1,estCostUSD:6,rating:3,description:`A former brick kiln telling how canals and water-powered silk mills made Bologna an industrial city, with working models that children enjoy.`,tip:`Opening days are limited, so check before going; it is a short bus ride north of the station.`,indoor:!0},{id:`via-d-azeglio`,name:`Via d'Azeglio`,category:`shopping`,tags:[`shopping`,`porticoes`,`passeggiata`,`free`],area:`Piazza Maggiore`,lat:44.49,lng:11.3419,durationHours:1,bestTime:[`afternoon`,`evening`],costLevel:0,estCostUSD:0,rating:3,description:`A pedestrian street of boutiques and cafés running south from Piazza Maggiore, at its best during the early-evening passeggiata.`,indoor:!1},{id:`modena-food-day-trip`,name:`Modena food day trip`,category:`food`,tags:[`day-trip`,`balsamic`,`parmigiano`,`unesco`,`tasting`],area:`Modena`,lat:44.64631,lng:10.92551,durationHours:7,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:3,estCostUSD:90,rating:5,description:`A short train ride to Modena for its Romanesque cathedral and Piazza Grande, with an early visit to a Parmigiano Reggiano dairy and a traditional balsamic vinegar acetaia.`,tip:`Dairies make cheese early, so book a tour that starts around 8am; trains from Bologna take about 30 minutes. Parma is a similar trip.`,indoor:!1,wiki:`Modena Cathedral`},{id:`ravenna-mosaics-day-trip`,name:`Ravenna mosaics day trip`,category:`culture`,tags:[`day-trip`,`mosaics`,`byzantine`,`unesco`,`rainy-day`],area:`Ravenna`,lat:44.42058,lng:12.19631,durationHours:7,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:30,rating:5,description:`Glittering 5th- and 6th-century mosaics in Ravenna's early Christian monuments, led by San Vitale and the starry Mausoleum of Galla Placidia.`,tip:`Trains take about 80 minutes; one combined ticket covers five monuments, and Galla Placidia needs a timed slot in busy months.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Basilica of San Vitale`},{id:`ferrari-museum-maranello`,name:`Ferrari Museum, Maranello`,localName:`Museo Ferrari Maranello`,category:`museum`,tags:[`cars`,`racing`,`day-trip`,`rainy-day`],area:`Maranello`,lat:44.52983,lng:10.8615,durationHours:5,bestTime:[`morning`,`afternoon`],costLevel:2,estCostUSD:35,rating:4,description:`Ferrari's showcase in its home town, full of Formula 1 cars, classic road cars and trophies, next to the factory and Fiorano test track.`,tip:`Go via Modena by train and the museum shuttle bus; combined tickets also cover the Enzo Ferrari museum in Modena.`,indoor:!0,wiki:`Museo Ferrari`}],foods:[{name:`Tagliatelle al Ragù`,description:`Golden egg ribbons tossed with Bologna's slow-cooked meat sauce; the real thing is never served on spaghetti.`},{name:`Tortellini in Brodo`,description:`Tiny navel-shaped pasta filled with pork loin, mortadella, prosciutto and Parmigiano, served in a rich capon or beef broth.`},{name:`Lasagne Verdi alla Bolognese`,localName:`Lasagne verdi alla bolognese`,description:`Spinach pasta sheets layered with ragù, béchamel and Parmigiano, baked until the edges crisp.`},{name:`Mortadella`,description:`Bologna's silky pork sausage studded with cubes of fat and sometimes pistachios, sliced paper-thin or cubed with aperitivo.`},{name:`Crescentine`,localName:`Crescentine fritte`,description:`Puffy squares of fried dough eaten hot with salumi, squacquerone cheese and cured meats on a shared board.`},{name:`Tortelloni with Butter and Sage`,localName:`Tortelloni burro e salvia`,description:`Large pasta parcels filled with ricotta, Parmigiano and parsley, glossed with melted butter and crisp sage.`}]}]};export{e as italy};